{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 229, "key": "FACT-0348: Lime1123 reports externally that division-specific handling is needed beyond detection recall, that their validation behaves as though division recove", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "Lime1123 reports externally that division-specific handling is needed beyond detection recall, that their validation behaves as though division recovery is especially sensitive inside roughly 3 um despite the official 7 um matcher, and that a high adjJ can coexist with a much lower divJ; Tang separately describes the productive order as detection, then linking, then division. These are competitor reports, not our measurements", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The reports are plausible and source-attributed, but no notebook, fold definition, matching census, or scorer artifact was supplied. The 3 um value is not an official metric threshold and must be treated as an empirical operating observation until reproduced on both P28 folds.", "value": "{'source': 'https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/biohub-cell-tracking-during-development/discussion/737543', 'lime_claims': ['division_specific_handling', 'effective_spatial_sensitivity_near_3um', 'detection_recall_not_sufficient'], 'tang_claim': ['detection_first', 'linking_second', 'division_third']}"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 230, "key": "FACT-0349: The patched division scorer has no special 3 um cutoff: it independently matches the predicted graph to each GT parent/divider/daughter/granddaughter ", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The patched division scorer has no special 3 um cutoff: it independently matches the predicted graph to each GT parent/divider/daughter/granddaughter window with the official 7 um DistanceMatching, then requires a local directed fork whose two predicted child branches map to two distinct GT daughter lineages. Therefore 7 um is only the admissibility radius; spatial errors well inside it can still change one-to-one assignments, branch identity and whether the whole division topology is recovered", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "7.0 micron_official_matching_radius"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 231, "key": "FACT-0350: The preregistered orthogonal-substrate sentinel did not establish P20/P19-to-P28 paired-delta equivalence on both folds: fold 0 met the fixed absolute", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The preregistered orthogonal-substrate sentinel did not establish P20/P19-to-P28 paired-delta equivalence on both folds: fold 0 met the fixed absolute tolerance, while the clean fold 1 exceeded it. The tested endpoint dedup rule also failed its own safety and promotion gates on every substrate, so this result licenses neither the rule nor inheritance of old-control deltas; independent levers must be scored directly on P28", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "False equivalent_both_folds"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 232, "key": "FACT-0351: The P29 DetPeak diagnostic passed its two-crop Kaggle smoke on the P28 champion pipeline: both non-empty sidecars reconstruct the detector's surviving", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The P29 DetPeak diagnostic passed its two-crop Kaggle smoke on the P28 champion pipeline: both non-empty sidecars reconstruct the detector's surviving peak counts exactly and the final graph is observationally identical to the matching P28 control rows. Repeated Kaggle console lines were not duplicate destination writes: the two GPU subprocesses receive disjoint step slices, and the race-safe create-if-absent sink observed no collision. Full two-fold passive exports are licensed; no score or submission claim is licensed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "True detpeak_smoke_pass"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 233, "key": "FACT-0352: Both full P29 DetPeak exports (EXP-0033/0034) are fetched and audited, and the DETECTION stage is bit-identical to the paired P28 champion controls on", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "Both full P29 DetPeak exports (EXP-0033/0034) are fetched and audited, and the DETECTION stage is bit-identical to the paired P28 champion controls on all 199 crops of both folds - the run_stats raw_nodes count agrees crop for crop. Fold 0 reproduces the champion graph exactly (71/71 crops, identical decompressed CSV); fold 1 reproduces 127 of 128, the single divergent crop differing by 5 nodes and 4 edges out of 3,778,768 rows with every counter up to and including DeepCenter and safe-division identical and the divergence confined to edge_prediction -> motion_relink -> short_track_filter. The sidecars therefore describe the P28 detection surface and are licensed for LEVER-0028 replay", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": null, "value": "True detection_contract_pass_both_folds"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 234, "key": "FACT-0353: The node deficit that LEVER-0028 targets is created by the ILP SOLVER, not by detection. On the P28 champion substrate the detector already emits at o", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The node deficit that LEVER-0028 targets is created by the ILP SOLVER, not by detection. On the P28 champion substrate the detector already emits at or above estimated_number_of_nodes on both folds (peaks-above-threshold / n_est median 1.0161 fold 0, 1.1331 fold 1); the ILP then discards 15.2% of them on fold 0 and 19.9% on fold 1, and only after that does the ratio fall to the cited under-count - post-ILP raw_nodes / n_est median 0.8884 on 44b6, reproducing dariushafshar's 0.888 figure EXACTLY at a stage the detection threshold cannot reach", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": null, "value": "0.8884 post_ilp_nodes_over_estimate_median_44b6"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 235, "key": "FACT-0354: The whole detection-threshold curve replayed on the P28 substrate shows almost no recall headroom below the deployed 0.96875: dropping to the export f", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The whole detection-threshold curve replayed on the P28 substrate shows almost no recall headroom below the deployed 0.96875: dropping to the export floor 0.5 admits 552,832 extra peaks on fold 0 to recover 20 more annotated cells (+0.00099 node recall, 0.9955 -> 0.9965) and 268,801 extra peaks on fold 1 to recover 2,396 (+0.02118, 0.9119 -> 0.9330), while driving N_pred/n_est from 0.89 to 1.10 (fold 0) and 1.20 to 1.33 (fold 1) deep into the over-prediction tax", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The recall numbers are sound. Node PRECISION and F1 from the same run are NOT interpretable and are not quoted: the annotated GT is sparse (861 cells against an estimate of 6362 on one crop), so most predicted nodes match no GT node by construction and the metric does not charge them as false positives.", "value": "0.00099 node_recall_gain_full_band_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 236, "key": "FACT-0355: The P28 pipeline LOSES annotated cells its own detector already found: node recall falls from 0.9955 to 0.9890 on fold 0 (133 cells net) and from 0.91", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The P28 pipeline LOSES annotated cells its own detector already found: node recall falls from 0.9955 to 0.9890 on fold 0 (133 cells net) and from 0.9119 to 0.8677 on fold 1 (5,000 cells net) between the detector's surviving peak set and the final champion graph, and on fold 1 the loss is one-directional - 126 of 128 crops lose, none gains. On the clean fold that retention loss is 2.1x everything the entire sub-threshold detection band could recover (FACT-0354)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "NET, not gross. Post-processing both removes nodes (ILP, isolated-node pruning, the short-track filter) and inserts them (synthetic gap nodes, safe divisions), and the intermediate graphs are not written to disk - only their counts are - so this does not attribute the net to a single stage. The final-graph recall here (0.9890 / 0.8677) is from a pure node matcher and is close to but NOT identical with the scorer's own node_recall in FACT-0345 (0.9868 / 0.8636); the definitions differ and FACT-0345 remains the scorer-authoritative figure. MAGNITUDE IS NOT A FORECAST (host, 2026-08-28). Fold 1 is leakage-clean but ASSOCIATION-DEGRADED (FACT-0261), and retention loss is downstream of association: a solver starved of good edges drops nodes for reasons the hidden leaderboard will not reproduce. Fold 1's 0.0442 is therefore strong DIAGNOSTIC evidence that the loss exists and where it sits, and NOT an estimate of what is recoverable in deployment. Fold 0's 0.0066 is the conservative figure and fold 0 remains the harder promotion gate.", "value": "0.0442 node_recall_lost_in_postprocessing_f1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 237, "key": "FACT-0356: The P28 node ledger closes EXACTLY on both folds and names where the nodes go: from the detector's surviving peaks, the ILP removes 354,243 (fold 0) a", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The P28 node ledger closes EXACTLY on both folds and names where the nodes go: from the detector's surviving peaks, the ILP removes 354,243 (fold 0) and 502,767 (fold 1), the short-track filter removes a further 93,044 / 104,078, isolated pruning removes 834 / 1,641, and synthetic gap closure adds back 21,037 / 16,628 - reproducing the final champion node count to the unit. The ILP is 79-83% of all node removal and the short-track filter 17-21%; safe divisions add EDGES, not nodes", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": null, "value": "0.791 ilp_share_of_node_removal_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 238, "key": "FACT-0357: The lost-cell atlas answers PKT-0025 falsifier (b) against a simple solver-blame reading: the ILP is mostly REACTING CORRECTLY to weak association, no", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The lost-cell atlas answers PKT-0025 falsifier (b) against a simple solver-blame reading: the ILP is mostly REACTING CORRECTLY to weak association, not needlessly discarding good cells. Of the 5,440 annotated cells fold 1 detects and then loses, 18.1% had NO candidate edge at all and a further 39.9% had a best candidate probability below 0.8, and the solver's drop rate falls monotonically with candidate quality - 51.1% of cells with no candidate are lost against 1.90% of those with a candidate above 0.99. The genuinely questionable decisions are the 1,300 lost cells (23.9%) whose best candidate exceeded 0.95. On FOLD 0, the promotion gate, the entire lost population is 176 cells of 20,107 (0.88%)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Two scope limits. (1) The candidate-edge columns require a pre-ILP graph, which exists only for fold 1 and comes from the 2026-08-19 export; that artifact is nodes-identical to P28 on all 128 crops and differs by at most one edge on 6 (FACT-0358), so it is used here as a description of the candidate set, not as a source of any paired delta (FACT-0350). (2) The atlas tracks GT CELLS, not node identity through the pipeline: \"kept\" means the annotated cell is still matched in the final graph, which post-processing can achieve with a synthetic gap node rather than the original peak. 942 KEPT cells had no candidate edge for exactly that reason.", "value": "0.181 share_of_lost_cells_with_no_candidate_edge_f1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 239, "key": "FACT-0358: The 2026-08-19 fold-1 pre-ILP export is substrate-equivalent to P28 at the pre-ILP stage: across all 128 crops its recorded post-ILP node count matche", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The 2026-08-19 fold-1 pre-ILP export is substrate-equivalent to P28 at the pre-ILP stage: across all 128 crops its recorded post-ILP node count matches P28's exactly, and its edge count matches on 122 of 128, differing by at most one edge on the remaining 6. The same +-1 edge jitter appears between P28 and P29 on an overlapping set of crops, so it is run-to-run pipeline nondeterminism and not a substrate difference", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "This establishes EQUIVALENCE OF THE CANDIDATE GRAPH, not licence to inherit results. FACT-0350 stands: no paired delta measured on the old controls may be carried to P28. What this fact permits is using the old pre-ILP artifact as the INPUT to a solver replay whose output is then compared against itself under different weights - a self-contained comparison in which the +-1 edge jitter is four orders of magnitude smaller than any promotable effect.", "value": "128 crops_with_identical_post_ilp_node_count"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 240, "key": "FACT-0359: Division failure on the P28 champion is TOPOLOGY-dominant, not detection-dominant: on fold 0, 22 of 26 GT division tuples (84.6%) have their divider a", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "Division failure on the P28 champion is TOPOLOGY-dominant, not detection-dominant: on fold 0, 22 of 26 GT division tuples (84.6%) have their divider and both daughters matched inside the official 7 um radius, yet only 22.7% of those fully-matched tuples are recovered by the official scorer - 17 of 22 fail with every member present. Fold 1 shows the same pattern at a lower matched rate (56.8% fully matched, 19.7% recovered). A tuple with any member unmatched is recovered 0% of the time in both folds", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Small n by nature - 151 GT divisions across both folds - so the RATES carry real sampling error even though the qualitative split does not. The 0% recovery for incomplete tuples is mechanically necessary (the scorer requires a matched parent and two distinct matched daughter branches), so it is a check that the instrument is wired correctly, not an independent finding.", "value": "0.2273 division_recovery_given_all_members_matched_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 241, "key": "FACT-0360: Lime1123's localisation observation (FACT-0348) REPRODUCES in direction on our data but is not established at our sample size: among division tuples w", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "Lime1123's localisation observation (FACT-0348) REPRODUCES in direction on our data but is not established at our sample size: among division tuples whose members are all matched inside the official 7 um radius, recovery is 0.333 when the worst member residual is under 3 um against 0.143 at or above it - an odds ratio of 3.0, same sign independently in both folds, with a bootstrap 95% CI on the difference of [+0.006, +0.387] that only just excludes zero and a two-sided Fisher exact p of 0.052", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "Direction is consistent and reproduces independently in both folds, but the evidence is thin: 93 fully-matched tuples, Fisher p = 0.052, and a bootstrap CI whose lower bound is +0.006. Two further caveats. The residual is computed by this module's own one-to-one match rather than read from the scorer's internal assignment, so it is a descriptive covariate on an official outcome. And 3 um is inherited from FACT-0348 as the band boundary rather than fitted, which avoids a fishing expedition but means the exact cut point is not itself evidence. Do NOT quote this as a validated threshold.", "value": "0.1905 division_recovery_difference_under_3um_pooled"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 242, "key": "FACT-0361: The StableDet/HOCT bundle is an ASSOCIATION-ONLY drop-in on our exact model contract, not an architecture port: its base edge predictor is bit-for-bit", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The StableDet/HOCT bundle is an ASSOCIATION-ONLY drop-in on our exact model contract, not an architecture port: its base edge predictor is bit-for-bit architecturally identical to the public pack's - 136 tensors, 2,077,996 parameters, identical key set and identical shapes - and its model card states the checkpoints score edges over detector-produced nodes with the same fixed downstream ILP. Its own config differs from ours in exactly one detector-side constant, pool_kernel_um 5.0 against our 3.0, with downsample [1,4,4] and window_size 2 shared", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": null, "value": "2077996 shared_edge_predictor_parameter_count"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 243, "key": "FACT-0362: The HOCT bundle explains WHY a strong association model can still have zero division recall, and it is a DATA limit rather than an architecture limit:", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The HOCT bundle explains WHY a strong association model can still have zero division recall, and it is a DATA limit rather than an architecture limit: its hard-negative checkpoint did train a fork head, on 327,265 supervised fork pairs containing only 110 POSITIVE examples - a 1:2975 imbalance carried by a pos_weight of 371.8 and a logit prior correction of 8.0 - and the published result was zero division recall in both held-out directions. Its PQLT and TOQL checkpoints additionally carry an explicit two-daughter decoder, a learned child_slots (2, 64) parameter", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The training-metadata values are read directly from the published checkpoints and are reliable as a record of what the publisher ran; the zero division recall is their own reported evaluation, which we have not reproduced. The causal claim - that 110 positives is WHY the fork head failed - is an inference from the imbalance, not a measured ablation. It is a strong inference, and it is testable.", "value": "110 positive_fork_training_pairs"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 244, "key": "FACT-0363: The deployed ILP has MULTIPLE OPTIMA and its edge solution is nondeterministic while its node solution is not. Three identical local solves of one cro", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The deployed ILP has MULTIPLE OPTIMA and its edge solution is nondeterministic while its node solution is not. Three identical local solves of one crop's pre-ILP graph, same file, same weights, same solver, returned 5,035 / 5,036 / 5,035 edges and 5,385 nodes every time; the three independently recorded Kaggle runs of the same crop recorded 5,036 / 5,035 / 5,036. This single mechanism explains the previously unattributed +-1 edge jitter in FACT-0352 and FACT-0358 - it is solver degeneracy, not GPU nondeterminism in edge prediction", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": null, "value": "5385 deterministic_node_count_across_solves"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 245, "key": "FACT-0364: The deployed champion DISCARDS the ILP's edge selection: motion_relink_edges replaces the whole edge list and re-assigns one-to-one per frame pair, an", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The deployed champion DISCARDS the ILP's edge selection: motion_relink_edges replaces the whole edge list and re-assigns one-to-one per frame pair, and on all 128 fold-1 crops it did so, covering a median 99.9% of the solver's raw edges with zero fallbacks. What survives the solver into the final graph is its NODE SET, not its edges. Any lever that improves the ILP's edge choice is therefore overwritten downstream and cannot be claimed for the champion without re-measuring through the relink", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": null, "value": "0.999 median_share_of_raw_edges_replaced_by_motion_relink_f1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 246, "key": "FACT-0365: The fold-1 solver sweep INVERTS LEVER-0035's direction: relaxing the disappearance weight loses monotonically (-0.0095 adjusted Jaccard at 0.1, CI exc", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The fold-1 solver sweep INVERTS LEVER-0035's direction: relaxing the disappearance weight loses monotonically (-0.0095 adjusted Jaccard at 0.1, CI excluding zero) while TIGHTENING it wins, peaking at 3.0 with +0.0085 adjusted and +0.0078 raw Jaccard, both CIs excluding zero, before collapsing at 8.0. The winning setting keeps 12.5% FEWER nodes than deployed (377,393 against 431,174) at essentially unchanged node recall (0.8232 against 0.8257) - the gain is selectivity, not retention", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "THE GAIN IS MEASURED ON A STAGE THE CHAMPION DISCARDS. The scored object is ILP output plus the short-track filter; the deployed pipeline replaces the ILP's entire edge list with motion relink on every crop (FACT-0364), so the edge-Jaccard gain that produced this result has no established transfer path. The NODE-set change does survive and is the part worth testing. Further limits: fold 1 only, 26 of 128 crops, and fold 1 is the association-degraded configuration (FACT-0261) while fold 0 is the promotion gate. Absolute scores here are not comparable to the champion's (FACT-0345). The 5.0 arm posted an adjusted gain with no raw gain and is flagged by the instrument as a count-adjustment artifact - an example of exactly what the separate reporting is for.", "value": "3.0 best_disappearance_weight_f1_pilot"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 247, "key": "FACT-0366: The deployed short-track filter length of 6 is already at its optimum on the fold-1 pilot: no tested alternative beats it, 8 and 10 are clearly worse ", "observed_at": "2026-08-28", "quote": "The deployed short-track filter length of 6 is already at its optimum on the fold-1 pilot: no tested alternative beats it, 8 and 10 are clearly worse on raw edge Jaccard with CIs excluding zero, and 2 and 4 are indistinguishable. Lengths 2 and 4 also show the count-adjustment signature in reverse - shortening the filter admits more nodes, which spends the under-production bonus (FACT-0191/0192) and turns a small raw gain at 4 into an adjusted loss", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "Same scope limits as FACT-0365: fold 1 only, 26 of 128 crops, and measured on ILP output rather than the deployed chain - the champion runs this filter AFTER motion relink (FACT-0364), on a different input graph, so these are the filter's properties in isolation.", "value": "6 best_min_track_len_f1_pilot"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 248, "key": "FACT-0367: The exact P28 full post-ILP chain is CPU-replayable from the existing local fold-1 pre-ILP export, raw images, and DeepCenter checkpoint. Five deploye", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The exact P28 full post-ILP chain is CPU-replayable from the existing local fold-1 pre-ILP export, raw images, and DeepCenter checkpoint. Five deployed-weight controls reproduced every predeclared stage count exactly. On a fixed 20-crop size-stratified panel, raising disappearance weight to 3.0 remained positive after motion relink, gap repair, DeepCenter vetoes, safe divisions, short-track filtering, line fitting, and the official scorer: the paired score delta was +0.0195 with a 95% crop-bootstrap interval +0.0007 to +0.0378. The mechanism was selectivity, removing 491 false edges while losing 84 true edges; signs split 10 positive / 10 negative crops", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "MAGNITUDE SUPERSEDED BY FACT-0372. The complete 128-crop fold-1 replay measured +0.0058 with a bootstrap interval INCLUDING zero, so this panel overstated the effect about 3.4x and its interval did not survive. Do not cite this fact's delta, its interval, or its edge TP/FP counts for anything. What still stands is the FEASIBILITY finding - the chain is CPU-replayable and the five deployed controls reproduced every predeclared stage count exactly - and the qualitative refutation of the FACT-0365 concern that motion relink necessarily erases any pre-relink gain. It was never a promotion result: fold 1 only, the panel deliberately size-stratified rather than the complete fold or a random sample, crop signs maximally heterogeneous, and FACT-0261 makes fold 0 the promotion gate. The old pre-ILP artifact is licensed for plumbing and mechanism measurement only, not leaderboard projection.", "value": "0.01950734925261588 full_chain_score_delta_f1_size_stratified_panel"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 249, "key": "FACT-0368: The ceiling ladder decomposes the remaining gap on the P28 substrate and ASSOCIATION DOMINATES BOTH FOLDS, overwhelmingly on the honest promotion fold", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The ceiling ladder decomposes the remaining gap on the P28 substrate and ASSOCIATION DOMINATES BOTH FOLDS, overwhelmingly on the honest promotion fold. Holding the deployed node set fixed and replacing only the edges with the best set those nodes admit raises raw edge Jaccard from 0.8862 to 0.9852 on all 71 fold-0 crops - 87.0% of the entire distance to a perfect graph - while perfect node SELECTION adds 5.9% and perfect DETECTION only 7.1%. Fold 1 gives the same ordering less extremely: association 54.0%, node selection 13.5%, detection 32.5%. Because rung 1 preserves the node count exactly, its ADJUSTED gain is count-fair: +0.1008 on fold 0 and +0.1591 on fold 1", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Fold 0 is the COMPLETE fold (71 of 71 crops); fold 1 is a stride-4 sample of 32 of 128. The harness verifies itself - perfect nodes with perfect edges score raw edge Jaccard exactly 1.0000 on both folds - so the rungs measure what they claim. Two limits on interpretation, both structural rather than statistical. (1) THE DECOMPOSITION IS SEQUENTIAL: the shares are attributed along one path (edges, then node selection, then detection) and a different order would apportion the overlap differently; the robust, order-independent reading is the association rung alone, which is measured against the deployed node set. (2) Rungs 2 and 3 restrict the prediction to ANNOTATED cells, which is far fewer nodes than the crop contains, so their ADJUSTED scores collect an under-production bonus (FACT-0191) that no real method can earn - they are read on raw edge Jaccard only, and the instrument flags them.", "value": "0.87 association_share_of_raw_jaccard_gap_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 250, "key": "FACT-0369: The deployed candidate-edge rule admits AT MOST ONE parent per target by construction, and this is verified both at source and in the data. `predict_u", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The deployed candidate-edge rule admits AT MOST ONE parent per target by construction, and this is verified both at source and in the data. `predict_unet_transformer.py` takes softmax over the SOURCE axis of the source-by-target logit matrix and keeps pairs above cfg.threshold = 0.5; since a softmax over sources sums to one, at most one source can exceed 0.5 for any target. Measured across all 2,162,040 fold-1 candidate edges the in-degree maximum is exactly 1 with zero exceptions, the minimum edge probability is exactly 0.5000, and only 85.7% of nodes have any candidate parent at all", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The mechanism is read at source and the consequence is independently confirmed in the exported candidate graph, which is the strongest available pairing. The degree census is fold 1 because that is the fold with a pre-ILP export, but the RULE is code shared by both folds, so the structural claim is not fold-specific; only the rates are.", "value": "1 max_candidate_parents_per_target"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 251, "key": "FACT-0370: Most but not all of the association ceiling is reachable by re-scoring today's candidate edges. Of the 109,057 fold-1 GT edges, 74.3% have a candidate", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "Most but not all of the association ceiling is reachable by re-scoring today's candidate edges. Of the 109,057 fold-1 GT edges, 74.3% have a candidate edge between their matched endpoints and would be recovered by a perfect scorer on the existing candidate set; 15.6% have BOTH endpoints detected yet no candidate edge at all; and 10.1% have an endpoint that was never detected. Restricted to GT edges whose endpoints are both detected, 82.7% are candidate-reachable. The unreachable ones are SHORT - median GT displacement 2.26 um - so they are missed by candidate SELECTION, not by any distance limit", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold-1 measurement, all 128 crops, using the official one-to-one 7 um matching shared with FACT-0354/0355/0357. Fold 0 has no pre-ILP export so the RATES are fold 1's; the candidate-generation rule they characterise (FACT-0369) is shared code, so the qualitative split is expected to hold on fold 0 while the numbers are not transferable to it.", "value": "0.827 share_of_detectable_gt_edges_that_are_candidate_reachable_f1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 252, "key": "FACT-0371: Divisions are not a separate capability axis - they are downstream of association. Perfecting ONLY the edges on the deployed fold-0 node set takes the", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "Divisions are not a separate capability axis - they are downstream of association. Perfecting ONLY the edges on the deployed fold-0 node set takes the division Jaccard from 0.0538 to 0.8462 (5 true positives and 67 false positives become 22 and 0) without touching detection or node selection. The full count-fair value of perfect association on today's nodes is therefore +0.1800 of SCORE on fold 0 - +0.1008 from the edge term and +0.0792 from the division term - and +0.2180 on fold 1. The deployed pipeline emits 67 false divisions on fold 0 against only 26 annotated ones", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Same instrument and scope as FACT-0368 - complete fold 0, stride-4 fold 1 - with the harness verified by its own rung 3. The arm holds the node set fixed, so both the adjusted edge term and the division term are directly comparable to deployed with no count-adjustment artifact. It is an ORACLE: the edges come from the ground truth, so correct fork topology is true by construction rather than learned.", "value": "0.18 count_fair_score_headroom_from_perfect_association_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 253, "key": "FACT-0372: The COMPLETE fold-1 full-chain replay does not reproduce the 20-crop panel: the tightened ILP selector (disappearance 3.0) scores +0.0058 over the P28", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The COMPLETE fold-1 full-chain replay does not reproduce the 20-crop panel: the tightened ILP selector (disappearance 3.0) scores +0.0058 over the P28 control across all 128 crops with a paired crop-bootstrap CI of [-0.0005, +0.0124] that INCLUDES ZERO, against the panel's +0.0195 with a CI excluding it - an overstatement of about 3.4x. Reported term by term as required: the RAW edge Jaccard gain is only +0.0013 while the adjusted gain is +0.0056, so 78% of the headline is the node-count adjustment and not tracking quality; node recall FALLS 0.8636 to 0.8359; and division true positives DROP from 14 to 12, the small division-Jaccard gain of +0.0015 coming entirely from 87 fewer false positives", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "This is the complete fold, all 128 crops, through the same AST-extracted chain whose deployed controls reproduced exactly (FACT-0367), with zero failed crops. It supersedes the 20-crop panel's MAGNITUDE, not its feasibility finding. Fold 1 remains association-degraded (FACT-0261) and is diagnostic rather than the promotion gate, so this neither promotes nor kills LEVER-0036 - only the honest fold-0 replay can.", "value": "0.005761347426969654 full_chain_score_delta_f1_complete"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 254, "key": "FACT-0373: The P30 fold-0 acquisition passed all four preregistered audits: it reproduced the P28 fold-0 control graph exactly (3,736,342 rows, byte-for-byte ide", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The P30 fold-0 acquisition passed all four preregistered audits: it reproduced the P28 fold-0 control graph exactly (3,736,342 rows, byte-for-byte identical columns), the edge-candidate patch reported its heartbeat on all 71 crops with both treatment variables unset, every one of the 1,973,714 deployed edges reappears in the export above the deployed threshold, and every exported candidate references a valid pre-ILP node id joining strictly consecutive frames. The acquisition surface is 6,630,491 candidates, 3.36x the deployed edge set", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Every check is fail-closed and each was declared in PKT-0027 before the run. Check A is the one that matters most for reuse: because the graph is identical to EXP-0030's, the P28 fold-0 control remains a valid pairing partner for both replays, and the acquisition did not change what it observes. Check D was added by the host precisely because counts and heartbeats can pass while an id-remapping boundary corrupts the surface; it is verified here on P30's own artifacts rather than inherited from the fold-1 observation that pre-ILP node k is the k-th surviving detector peak.", "value": "True p30_acquisition_audit_passed"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 255, "key": "FACT-0374: Candidate reach on the honest fold is far higher than fold 1 suggested, so LEVER-0037's headroom on the promotion fold is about a third of what FACT-0", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "Candidate reach on the honest fold is far higher than fold 1 suggested, so LEVER-0037's headroom on the promotion fold is about a third of what FACT-0370 implied. Across all 71 fold-0 crops and 19,665 detectable GT edges, the DEPLOYED rule already offers 93.9% of them, against 82.7% on fold 1. The true parent sits at rank 1 for 95.7% of edges and within rank 2 for 99.3%, so rank beyond 2 buys almost nothing. The smallest expansion that materially improves reach is floor 0.1 with at most 2 parents per target: 98.6% reach for 1.4x the candidate count", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold 0, all 71 crops, on the P30 acquisition whose four audits passed (FACT-0373) - including the node-id check that guarantees these candidates address the same nodes the pre-ILP graph consumes. Reach is an UPPER BOUND: it counts GT edges whose true pair is OFFERED, not chosen. A scorer still has to pick the right parent out of the widened set, and widening necessarily hands the linker more ways to be wrong, so the realised gain will be smaller and could be negative. SELECTION DEPENDENCY (host red-team, 2026-08-29): the treatment floor and rank were CHOSEN from this fold-0 GT reach surface, and LEVER-0037 is then scored on that same fold. The resulting replay is TREATMENT CHARACTERISATION, not an independent confirmation, and no fold-0 number from it may be presented as out-of-sample. A positive result licenses a frozen fold-1 acquisition and replay, or - if submission economics warrant it - one cautiously preregistered leaderboard test. It does not license automatic promotion. NOT A SCORE CEILING: the unreachable-edge percentage is a share of DETECTABLE GT EDGES, not a bound on the score. It must never be reinterpreted as one - the score passes through the linker, the count adjustment and the division term, none of which this quantity touches.", "value": "0.939 deployed_candidate_reach_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 256, "key": "FACT-0375: LEVER-0036 FAILS its own preregistered fold-0 gate on every criterion. Across all 71 fold-0 crops through the complete champion chain, the tightened I", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "LEVER-0036 FAILS its own preregistered fold-0 gate on every criterion. Across all 71 fold-0 crops through the complete champion chain, the tightened ILP selector scores +0.00288 - below the +0.003 bar - with a paired bootstrap interval of [-0.0018, +0.0077] that INCLUDES ZERO, and its RAW edge Jaccard is NEGATIVE at -0.00084 while the adjusted figure is +0.00264. The entire apparent gain is the node-count adjustment. Node recall falls 0.9868 to 0.9782 and division true positives are unchanged at 5", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The complete honest fold, all 71 crops, zero failed crops, on the P30 substrate whose four audits passed (FACT-0373) and through a chain whose fold-0 deployed controls replay exactly. This closes LEVER-0036 on evidence ABOUT ITSELF, as the one-lever-one-evidence rule requires - not by inheritance from the fold-1 result (FACT-0372), which merely predicted it.", "value": "0.0028771828701325 full_chain_score_delta_f0_complete"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 257, "key": "FACT-0376: LEVER-0037 is a RANKING FAILURE, not a candidate-generation win. Widening the fold-0 candidate set to floor 0.1 with at most two parents per target ra", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "LEVER-0037 is a RANKING FAILURE, not a candidate-generation win. Widening the fold-0 candidate set to floor 0.1 with at most two parents per target raised GT-edge reach from 18,466 to 19,390 of 19,665 detectable edges - 924 newly reachable pairs at 1.45x the candidates - and the complete chain converted only 28 of them into net true edges, a 3.0% conversion, while adding 113 false-positive edges. The score FALLS 0.00906 with a bootstrap interval of [-0.0154, -0.0034] that excludes zero, raw edge Jaccard falls 0.00339, and division true positives drop from 5 to 4. Node retention DID improve as the mechanism predicted (recall 0.9868 to 0.9900, +156,408 nodes) - the extra edges do retain nodes, but the linker cannot pick the right parents from the wider set", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The NEGATIVE result is solid - complete fold 0, 71 crops, interval excluding zero, and the treatment was selected to be favourable to the lever, so a loss under its own best setting is strong evidence. Two limits on the MECHANISM claim. (1) delta_edge_tp is a NET count: the replay retains per-crop metrics and not final graphs, so 28 net could be 28 gained and 0 lost, or hundreds gained and nearly as many displaced. PKT-0027 rule (5) triggers an identity-level re-run that persists graphs before the ranking diagnosis is treated as established. (2) The floor and rank were chosen on this same fold's GT reach (FACT-0374), so this is treatment characterisation; that selection bias worked IN THE LEVER'S FAVOUR, which makes the negative result more, not less, credible.", "value": "0.0303 newly_reachable_gt_edge_conversion_rate_f0"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 258, "key": "FACT-0377: The public kernel stephennedumpally/pls-upvote-share-higher-scoring-ideas, reported at 0.931 and therefore ABOVE our 0.928 champion, is the SAME code ", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The public kernel stephennedumpally/pls-upvote-share-higher-scoring-ideas, reported at 0.931 and therefore ABOVE our 0.928 champion, is the SAME code lineage as ours and differs from the P24/P28 champion by ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES ONLY - every code path it exercises is already present in our P28 control notebook. Its two substantive additions are association-DISCRIMINATION mechanisms our champion leaves switched off: a secondary model blended through `low_margin_consensus`, and bidirectional harmonic-probability fusion at weight 0.15. It also runs a tighter ILP (disappearance 2.0, division 1.2) and turns on gap-2 recovery and adaptive short-track rescue", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "MATERIALLY CORRECTED 2026-08-29, SAME DAY, BEFORE ANY RUN WAS READ. The claim that the secondary low_margin_consensus is an addition \"our champion leaves switched off\" is WRONG. The deployed P24 champion ALREADY runs it, with identical parameters - link mode low_margin_consensus, edge weight 0.15, low-margin max 0.35, detection weight 0.475, dual-seed edge threshold 0.48 - verified in notebooks/kaggle_p24_deepcenter_best_veto/. The LOEO controls (P28) only appear to lack it because the harness applies a contamination cut for the champion arm (FACT-0378); the DEPLOYED artifact has it on. THE ACTUAL DIFF between P24 (0.928) and the public 0.931 is therefore narrower and is listed under scope.corrected_diffs. The one genuine association-side difference is the bidirectional FUSION MODE: P24 uses a plain linear blend at weight 0.20 and contains no harmonic_probability code at all, while the public kernel uses harmonic-probability fusion at 0.15. Everything else that differs is solver, detector threshold, or post-processing. The CONFIGURATION of the public kernel remains VERIFIED - read directly from the pulled notebook source at C:/temp/intel/sn931/code.py, and the corresponding code paths are confirmed present in our own P28 control notebook. The SCORE 0.931 is the host's report of the public leaderboard and has not been independently reproduced by us; it is also a public-LB number, so the usual public/private caveat applies. No claim here is that their configuration will score 0.931 on OUR substrate - that is what the paired offline runs are for.", "value": "0.931 reported_public_lb_score"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 259, "key": "FACT-0378: The secondary model used by the FACT-0377 public configuration exists ONLY as split_0 - the biohub-temporal-unet3d-seed314159-v1 pack manifest contain", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The secondary model used by the FACT-0377 public configuration exists ONLY as split_0 - the biohub-temporal-unet3d-seed314159-v1 pack manifest contains two split_0 references and zero split_1 - and the notebook hardcodes SECONDARY_WEIGHTS_PATH to unet_transformer/split_0/edge_predictor_best.pth. Because our LOEO protocol treats pack split_0 as CLEAN for fold 0, that model trained on 6bba; fold 1 holds 6bba out. Enabling the secondary consensus on fold 1 therefore LEAKS the held-out embryo, and no honest fold-1 secondary exists to substitute", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Established two ways: the pack's ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.json has no split_1 entry at all, and the base notebook's hardcoded path is read at source. The leak direction follows from our own protocol (FACT-0345), which uses pack split_0 as the CLEAN fold-0 primary and OOF split_1 for fold 1 precisely to keep that guard - so pack split_0 is a model that saw 6bba.", "value": "0 honest_loeo_folds_for_the_secondary_checkpoint"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 260, "key": "FACT-0379: The pool_kernel_um mismatch recorded as LEVER-0034's integration blocker is NOT REAL. `load_model` reads config.json - including its pool_kernel_um 5.", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The pool_kernel_um mismatch recorded as LEVER-0034's integration blocker is NOT REAL. `load_model` reads config.json - including its pool_kernel_um 5.0 - but returns only (model, window_size, downsample) and never applies that field, so peak extraction runs at the PredictConfig dataclass default of 3.0 on every run of this predictor. Our deployed fold-0 log confirms it prints pool_kernel_um=3.0 while the loaded pack config says 5.0. Because HOCT's model card states it used the fixed OFFICIAL predicted nodes from this same codebase, its training node surface was extracted at 3.0 as well: the upstream node contract MATCHES ours", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Established at source and confirmed in a deployed run log, which is the strongest pairing available. The inference for HOCT is one step weaker but well grounded: their own model card says they scored edges over fixed official predicted nodes from this codebase, and this codebase cannot apply a 5.0 pool at inference. It would be falsified if HOCT turned out to have regenerated nodes with a patched predictor, which nothing in the published artifacts suggests.", "value": "3.0 effective_pool_kernel_um_at_inference"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 261, "key": "FACT-0380: Division tuples are systematically WORSE LOCALISED than ordinary matched cells on both folds, reproducing a competitor's independent observation. On f", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "Division tuples are systematically WORSE LOCALISED than ordinary matched cells on both folds, reproducing a competitor's independent observation. On fold 0, 45.5% of GT division tuples have a member beyond 3 um while all members pass the official 7 um matcher, against 12.0% of all matched cells - a 3.8x enrichment; on fold 1 it is 74.6% against 37.3%. Median worst-member residual is 2.841 um (f0) and 3.723 um (f1) against 1.675 and 2.298 for matched cells generally. Kaggle user kevin park reported 39% of their division nodes outside 3 um while passing 7 um; our fold-0 figure is 45.5%", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The localisation figures are our own, computed from committed instruments over the complete folds, and the fold-0 division sample is small (22 fully-matched tuples) so its RATE carries real sampling error even though the enrichment direction is clear on both folds. The competitor numbers are EXTERNAL and unverified - forum-reported, no artifact - and their adjJ/divJ are on their own validation, not the same folds as ours, so they calibrate the shape of a frontier score and must not be compared to our offline numbers as if measured alike.", "value": "0.455 share_of_f0_division_tuples_with_a_member_beyond_3um"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 262, "key": "FACT-0381: The parent-discrimination task, measured on the frozen target-wise surface over the honest fold, is far smaller and far harder than the aggregate sugg", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The parent-discrimination task, measured on the frozen target-wise surface over the honest fold, is far smaller and far harder than the aggregate suggests. Of 19,444 fold-0 decidable targets - those whose true parent is actually among the candidates - only 4,157 (21.4%) are CONTESTED, i.e. offered more than one candidate parent; on the other 78.6% top-1 is 1.0 by construction. Deployed top-1 is 0.9645 overall but 0.8338 on contested targets, leaving 691 wrong parent choices as the entire learnable headroom of this task on fold 0. The equivalent fold-1 figure is DEGENERATE and must not be quoted: without a richer candidate export that fold has exactly one candidate per target (FACT-0369), so its top-1 is 1.0 by arithmetic", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold 0, all 71 crops, through the frozen label contract in scripts/win_bet/assoc_parent_dataset.py - one-to-one 7 um matching shared with FACT-0354/0355/0357, targets whose true parent was never offered scored separately rather than charged to the scorer. The task is measured only on ANNOTATED targets with ANNOTATED parents, which is what the metric rewards; edges among unannotated cells are outside it by construction.", "value": "0.8338 deployed_parent_top1_on_contested_targets_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 263, "key": "FACT-0382: The contested parent-choice population is a property of the ACQUISITION FLOOR, not of the deployed pipeline, and at the deployed floor BOTH folds are ", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The contested parent-choice population is a property of the ACQUISITION FLOOR, not of the deployed pipeline, and at the deployed floor BOTH folds are degenerate. Restricting the fold-0 frozen surface to the deployed candidate rule (edge probability > 0.5) leaves a maximum of ONE candidate per target and ZERO contested targets - identical to fold 1 - so deployed parent top-1 is 1.0 by arithmetic on the surface the pipeline actually consumes. The 4,157 contested targets of FACT-0381 exist only because the P30 export widened the surface to floor 0.1; the count falls monotonically with the floor (0.10 -> 4,157; 0.20 -> 1,800; 0.30 -> 757; 0.40 -> 268; 0.50 -> 0). Decisively, ALL 691 of the contested errors have their true parent at probability <= 0.5, median 0.2679, so not one of them is offered to the deployed pipeline at all", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Computed over the complete fold-0 frozen surface, all 71 crops, from the same committed table (C:/temp/assoc/f0.parquet) that produced FACT-0381, by filtering on the deployed rule verified at source in FACT-0369. It uses no new matcher, no new label contract and no new candidate export, so it cannot disagree with FACT-0381 about anything except the framing it corrects.", "value": "0 contested_fold0_targets_at_the_deployed_candidate_floor"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 264, "key": "FACT-0383: The division population, measured through the OFFICIAL scorer on both complete folds, is far smaller than the emitted fork population and almost all o", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "The division population, measured through the OFFICIAL scorer on both complete folds, is far smaller than the emitted fork population and almost all of it is invisible to the metric. Fold 0 emits 5,656 predicted forks of which the metric charges only 72 - 5 true positives and 67 false - so 98.7% are ignored; fold 1 emits 5,582 of which 363 are charged. The complete fold-1 census, never previously measured (FACT-0371 used a 32-crop subset), is 125 annotated divisions with 14 TP / 349 FP / 111 FN. The class a verifier must actually learn is therefore EMITTED TRUE FORKS - 5 on fold 0 and 14 on fold 1, nineteen in total - not the 26 and 125 annotated divisions", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Both folds complete - 71 and 128 crops - through the scorer's OWN matcher rather than a second one: populations come from score_divisions (whose fp_forks IS the metric's false-positive tally), _pred_division_fork_sets and _match_full at 7 um, and every crop RAISES unless it reconciles with tracking_cellmot.metrics.evaluate. The fold-0 counts reproduce FACT-0375's control arm exactly, which is an independent check that this census and the deployed scorer count the same events.", "value": "0.9873 share_of_f0_emitted_forks_the_metric_ignores"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 265, "key": "FACT-0384: A PERFECT false-fork verifier is worth +0.01416 of score on fold 0 and +0.00817 on fold 1 - 2.4x the prize LEVER-0040 estimated - and its edits are ne", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "A PERFECT false-fork verifier is worth +0.01416 of score on fold 0 and +0.00817 on fold 1 - 2.4x the prize LEVER-0040 estimated - and its edits are net-POSITIVE on the edge term rather than a cost. Rejecting every fold-0 fork the official scorer calls a false positive, deleting the weakest child edge of each, takes division false positives 67 to 0 with true positives held at 5, division Jaccard 0.0538 to 0.1923, and RAW edge Jaccard UP from 0.886247 to 0.886557 because 39 false edges go with the 28 true ones. The adapter that measures this reproduces the deployed division counts EXACTLY at 5 / 67 / 21 and agrees with exact re-scoring on 142 of 142 fold-0 and 256 of 256 fold-1 crop-rungs", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The SELECTION is an oracle - it uses the scorer's own verdict about which forks are false - so this is a CEILING and never a result. The division counts and the edge cost it reports are real, computed by the official scorer over the complete folds. The adapter's credential is that it reproduces a known number: rung 1, with zero rejections, returns the deployed 5 / 67 / 21 exactly, so the machinery that measures the ceiling is the machinery that reproduces the control.", "value": "0.01416236257517689 perfect_false_fork_verifier_score_ceiling_f0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 266, "key": "FACT-0385: A cross-fitted false-fork verifier is DATA-LIMITED, not architecture-limited, and it INVERTS between embryos. Trained on fold 1's emitted forks - 14 p", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "A cross-fitted false-fork verifier is DATA-LIMITED, not architecture-limited, and it INVERTS between embryos. Trained on fold 1's emitted forks - 14 positives - and judged on the fold it never saw, it rejects 14 of 67 fold-0 false positives before losing a single true positive, a deployment-view AUC of 0.6299 worth roughly +0.001 of score against FACT-0384's +0.01416 ceiling. The same protocol judged on fold 1 rejects only 5 of 349 before the first true-positive loss, BELOW the random expectation of 23.3. Two design traps were found and disarmed: pooling GT-derived tuples with emitted forks inflates the unseen-fold AUC to 0.8006 while the deployment view is 0.5254, because out_degree and competing_parents read the CONSTRUCTION ROUTE rather than the physics; and the Zebrahub external positives are ANTI-ALIGNED with our surface at pooled AUC 0.179, collapsing an in-domain fit from 0.80 to 0.21", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The NEGATIVE is solid and the protocol is sound - the cross-fit is enforced mechanically by a single selector with an assertion that raises on a judged-fold row, on the held-out embryo when the fold column lies, and on any identifier reaching the feature list. What makes it SUSPECT rather than VALID is sample size in the only place it matters: the fold-0 result rests on 5 true positives and 67 false ones, so 14-of-67 carries very wide sampling error, and the fold-1 arm rests on 14 positives. A result built on nineteen positives across both folds is not a stable estimate of anything.", "value": "14 f0_false_forks_rejected_before_the_first_true_positive_loss"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 267, "key": "FACT-0386: Simple models on the existing representation-free features CANNOT beat the deployed edge probability at choosing parents, and the small apparent gain ", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "Simple models on the existing representation-free features CANNOT beat the deployed edge probability at choosing parents, and the small apparent gain is mostly a discretisation artifact. Across 22 preregistered crop-grouped arms on the complete fold-0 frozen surface, the LINEAR model never beats the deployed 0.8338 on contested targets at any feature set, and the best TREE arm reaches 0.8367 - a point gain of +0.0029, net +12 targets of the 691 available with churn 40 - with a crop-paired interval of [-0.00051, +0.00644] that includes zero and McNemar p = 0.081. NO ARM OF THE 22 HAS A FAVOURABLE INTERVAL. The noise floor was measured rather than assumed: a tree given ONLY the deployed probability, which cannot in principle beat an argmax over that same scalar, still posts +0.0014 and net +6 because the learner bins each feature into at most 255 quantile bins and 41 contested targets have candidates colliding in a bin - so the best arm's +12 is roughly twice a pure-binning floor of +6", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold 0, all 71 crops, out-of-fold only, splits GROUPED BY CROP so no target contributes to its own training fold, with leave-one-crop-out reported as the strictest available proxy and agreeing with the 5-fold result. All 22 arms were preregistered and ALL 22 are reported, so there is no best-of-many selection. The harness carries its own internal control: a LINEAR model on the probability alone returns exactly the deployed number with churn 0, which is what a monotone transform of a single feature must do to an argmax - so the tree's +0.0014 on the same input is demonstrably binning and not skill. The run was repeated end to end after the tie-break correction landed and both runs agree on all 22 arms with zero disagreements.", "value": "0.8366610536444551 best_tree_contested_parent_top1_f0_oof"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 268, "key": "FACT-0387: PKT-0029 Gate 1 FAILED, and it failed at a PROCESS BOUNDARY rather than on parity. The feature-parity smoke raised ModuleNotFoundError on `import pred", "observed_at": "2026-08-29", "quote": "PKT-0029 Gate 1 FAILED, and it failed at a PROCESS BOUNDARY rather than on parity. The feature-parity smoke raised ModuleNotFoundError on `import predict_unet_transformer`, compared ZERO crops, and reported all_passed false. The cause is structural, not a typo: the deployed edge predictor is never imported into the notebook process at all - it is launched as a SUBPROCESS, `/usr/bin/python3 scripts/predict_unet_transformer.py`, with the repo directory as its working directory, and every patch in this tree that has ever worked reaches it by REWRITING THAT FILE'S SOURCE TEXT rather than importing the module. The parity patch was the only one that tried to import it, from a process where its directory is not on sys.path", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Re-derived at file:line from the fetched kernel log and the retained gate report, not inferred: the traceback names the import, the report records zero crops with all_passed false, and the same log shows the pipeline immediately afterwards launching the module as a subprocess with a relative path. The contrast with the patches that DO work - pre_ilp_export.py and edge_candidate_budget.py, both of which ran cleanly in P30 - is visible in their source: they never import, they rewrite.", "value": "0 crops_compared_by_the_gate_1_parity_smoke"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 269, "key": "FACT-0388: The fold-1 candidate acquisition INVERTS which fold holds the parent-ranking headroom. On the widened surface P34 delivered, fold 1 has 91,410 decidab", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The fold-1 candidate acquisition INVERTS which fold holds the parent-ranking headroom. On the widened surface P34 delivered, fold 1 has 91,410 decidable targets of which 26,601 are CONTESTED - a 29.1% contested share against fold 0's 21.4% - with deployed contested top-1 of only 0.7084 and 7,757 wrong parent choices. That is 6.4x fold 0's contested population and 11.2x its errors, at a materially LOWER deployed accuracy. PKT-0030's falsifier (e), that fold 1 might remain too degenerate to falsify a ranker, does NOT fire; the opposite is true and fold 1 is now the richer evaluation surface", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold 1, all 128 crops, produced by the SAME committed instrument that produced FACT-0381 and FACT-0386 - scripts/win_bet/assoc_parent_dataset.py through its frozen label contract - so the two folds are directly comparable rather than merely adjacent. The substrate passed audits B, C and D on all 128 crops before the census was computed, and its pre-ILP export is byte-identical to the 2026-08-19 preilp_f1_v2 parquet with the sha256 recomputed in-run rather than inherited.", "value": "0.7083944212623585 deployed_parent_top1_on_contested_targets_f1_widened"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 270, "key": "FACT-0389: The P34 fold-1 acquisition reproduces the P28 champion control on 127 of 128 crops and diverges on exactly one - 6bba_e16ffc58 at +5 nodes and +4 edge", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The P34 fold-1 acquisition reproduces the P28 champion control on 127 of 128 crops and diverges on exactly one - 6bba_e16ffc58 at +5 nodes and +4 edges - and the acquisition is NOT the cause. The same crop with the same deltas was recorded by FACT-0352 under a completely different patch, and P34's decompressed graph is BYTE-IDENTICAL to P29's, so two independently patched runs agree with each other and disagree with P28. The mechanism is ILP degeneracy amplified by a filter threshold: detection is bit-identical everywhere, raw ILP edges differ on 5 crops, and on this crop the extra edge changes which components fall under OUTPUT_MIN_TRACK_LEN 6, moving short_track_components_removed from 61 to 62", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The attribution is what makes this VALID rather than merely observed: it was tested against a THIRD run. If the acquisition had caused the divergence, P34 would differ from P29 as well as from P28; it is byte-identical to P29, which leaves P28's own solver draw as the only common factor. The per-stage run_stats then name the mechanism rather than leaving it inferred.", "value": "1 crops_of_128_where_p34_diverges_from_the_p28_fold1_control"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 271, "key": "FACT-0390: PKT-0029's central premise was FALSE - the HOCT publisher DID ship model code, so the feature contract is READ rather than inferred. Their own LICENSE", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "PKT-0029's central premise was FALSE - the HOCT publisher DID ship model code, so the feature contract is READ rather than inferred. Their own LICENSES.md names the dataset rudispresence/biohub-stabledet-hoct-code, which exists and ships repo_overlay/methods/stabledet_hoct_fork/hoct_edge_transformer.py under MIT. Their class StableDetHOCTFork(feature_dim=32) strict-loads BOTH published checkpoints at 447,376 parameters, and our rebuilt module now reproduces its edge and quiet logits at a maximum absolute delta of EXACTLY 0.000e+00 on both folds. The two-fold GPU contract-ranking tournament the packet planned is not needed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Re-derived this cycle by running both modules on the same inputs and differencing their logits, not by reading either. The delta is exactly zero rather than merely small, on both folds and on both output heads, which is what distinguishes \"we found the producing source\" from \"we found something that scores similarly\". The publisher source and the licence file are on disk at the named paths.", "value": "0.0 max_abs_logit_delta_between_our_module_and_the_publisher_class"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 272, "key": "FACT-0391: A strict state-dict load is NECESSARY AND DEMONSTRABLY NOT SUFFICIENT to recover a model. The earlier HOCT reconstruction strict-loaded both checkpoin", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "A strict state-dict load is NECESSARY AND DEMONSTRABLY NOT SUFFICIENT to recover a model. The earlier HOCT reconstruction strict-loaded both checkpoints at exactly the right parameter count and still computed the WRONG FUNCTION in three independent ways, none of which changes any tensor shape and so none of which strict=True can see: ReLU where the publisher uses GELU, norm_first False where the publisher uses True, and a 3-D rotary position embedding applied to queries and keys at edge midpoints OMITTED ENTIRELY - the last being invisible to any checkpoint because its frequencies are a persistent=False buffer that is never serialised", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Established by construction rather than by argument: with the three divergences present the module strict-loaded and produced different logits; with them corrected it reproduces the publisher exactly on both folds. The claim is pinned by a named test rather than left as prose.", "value": "3 silent_function_divergences_surviving_a_strict_load"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 273, "key": "FACT-0392: The binding HOCT integration mismatch is the CANDIDATE SURFACE, not the detector, and it is larger than the pool-kernel blocker it replaces. HOCT's ca", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The binding HOCT integration mismatch is the CANDIDATE SURFACE, not the detector, and it is larger than the pool-kernel blocker it replaces. HOCT's candidate rule is a purely geometric 15 um ball over every source, uncapped and unfiltered; our deployed rule admits at most ONE parent per target by arithmetic (FACT-0369) and the widened P30 surface at most four. The head was trained to discriminate among competitors our pipeline never offers, so it CANNOT be run as a reranker of our candidate list - it must be given its own 15 um graph rebuilt from node coordinates. Its probabilities also carry an abstain mass ours lacks, so only WITHIN-TARGET RANKING is comparable and absolute levels never are", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Both rules were read at named file:line in the publisher's own code and in ours, rather than inferred from behaviour. The consequence - that within-target ranking is the only comparable quantity - follows from the abstain mass being present on one side and absent on the other, which is also read at source.", "value": "15.0 hoct_candidate_gate_um_uncapped_vs_our_one_parent_rule"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 274, "key": "FACT-0393: The PKT-0028 bridge submission scored 0.931 on the public leaderboard, above the 0.928 P24 champion (FACT-0341) and at the top of its preregistered 0.", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The PKT-0028 bridge submission scored 0.931 on the public leaderboard, above the 0.928 P24 champion (FACT-0341) and at the top of its preregistered 0.925-0.932 band. The falsifier - a score at or below 0.928 - did NOT fire, so the public lineage reproduces on our account and the campaign's baseline relocates from 0.928 to 0.931. This is BASELINE RELOCATION AND NOT NEW CAPABILITY, which PKT-0028's interpretation rule (2) preregistered before the run: the configuration is run byte-identical, every knob in it is confounded, and nothing about our own association or division capability changed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read from the official leaderboard through the established submissions path, status COMPLETE, on a notebook run byte-identical to the public source. The number is the competition's own, not ours. What it does NOT establish is anything about mechanism - see the note.", "value": "0.931 public_lb_score_of_the_exact_public_configuration"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 275, "key": "FACT-0394: Gate 1's in-kernel pass condition is VACUOUS ON BAND A, so a crop that compared zero deployed-band pairs is reported as passing. The gate floors band ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "Gate 1's in-kernel pass condition is VACUOUS ON BAND A, so a crop that compared zero deployed-band pairs is reported as passing. The gate floors band B at a non-zero comparison count but floors band A at nothing, so with no recorded band-A edge in scope the three band-A conditions - no missing, no extra, delta within tolerance - are all satisfied trivially. The defect did not need manufacturing to demonstrate: the repository's own GREEN test test_gate_passes_when_the_cache_is_faithful already ran a crop whose band A compared ZERO pairs and asserted all_passed True, so the band-A comparison path was never exercised by the suite that was meant to prove it", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Demonstrated by running BOTH workers against one identical fixture rather than by reading either. Band B still compares 27 pairs under the patched worker, which is what proves the refusal is the band-A floor and not a collateral band-B failure. The committed worker's behaviour is not inferred from the source - it was executed.", "value": "0 band_a_pairs_compared_by_a_crop_the_committed_gate_reports_as_passing"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 276, "key": "FACT-0395: The fold-hygiene guard was blind to specs that INHERIT their fold from a base notebook, and the blind spot covered the fold-1 acquisition we just cons", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The fold-hygiene guard was blind to specs that INHERIT their fold from a base notebook, and the blind spot covered the fold-1 acquisition we just consumed. kaggle_factory.apply_edit APPENDS a spec's env block after the base notebook's existing text, so any os.environ the base carries stays in force unless the spec names the same key - and the guard read the fold from the spec env alone. Resolving the EFFECTIVE fold takes fold-1 coverage from 12 specs to 14 and fold-0 from 19 to 22. Both newly visible fold-1 specs, p29_p28_detpeak_export_f1 and p34_acquisition_f1, are CLEAN, so this closes a hole rather than retracting a result", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The before-figures reproduce the independent PKT-0036 measurement of 12 checked and 54 skipped exactly, which is what makes the after-figures a like-for-like closure rather than a differently-counted set. Seven mutation tests reach the EXP-0019 defect through the inheritance route specifically and require the guard to fire on each.", "value": "14 fold1_specs_checked_by_the_hygiene_guard_after_resolving_the_effective_fold"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 277, "key": "FACT-0396: The champion transition from P24 to P32 is RELEASED on a bound receipt, 26 of 26 conditions, and it is a transition between TWO FULLY BOUND ARTIFACTS.", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The champion transition from P24 to P32 is RELEASED on a bound receipt, 26 of 26 conditions, and it is a transition between TWO FULLY BOUND ARTIFACTS. P32 binds notebook 856451d8, submission graph e7ee404d, upstream cell-source de60a4f0, kernel version 1, with the public source kernel re-pulled and its ten cell sources byte-identical to the executed notebook. P24 passes its own receipt 25 of 25 from C:/temp/queue/p24_deepcenter_best_veto/, where a complete passing set has sat since 2026-08-27", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Every condition was exercised rather than asserted: the receipt harness plants 16 defects across 19 tests - float coordinates, illegal in-degree, mutated graph, notebook edited after build, slug divergence, smuggled dataset, spec edited after audit, score outside band, fired falsifier, registry disagreement, upstream divergence, an applicable defect rule not recorded, and four fail-closed cases - and each is caught by its OWN named condition rather than by a generic failure.", "value": "26 release_receipt_conditions_passed_by_p32_of_26"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 278, "key": "FACT-0397: Gate 1 attempt 2 (EXP-0041, kernel version 2) FAILED at t=238 s with ZERO crops compared, for the second attempt running, and the cause was a hardcode", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "Gate 1 attempt 2 (EXP-0041, kernel version 2) FAILED at t=238 s with ZERO crops compared, for the second attempt running, and the cause was a hardcoded dataset mount root. The patch looked up /kaggle/input/biohub-identity-replay-f0/... while Kaggle mounted the dataset at /kaggle/input/datasets/<owner>/<slug>/... - the string \"identity\" appears ZERO times in the run's log. The dataset itself was correct and attached. THE TRAP AND ITS FIX WERE ALREADY WRITTEN DOWN IN THE SAME DIRECTORY, in a file this very notebook loads: scripts/kaggle_edits/loeo_retarget.py:86-101 records the identical failure from 2026-08-01, where a fold-1 kernel died at t=628 s for the same reason, and ships the bounded depth ladder that fixes it", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read from the fetched run's own report and log rather than inferred: the report records zero crops with all_passed false, the traceback names the raise, and a grep of the log finds the dataset slug zero times while the three pilkwang datasets appear at the nested root. The precedent files were read at the named lines.", "value": "0 crops_compared_by_gate_1_attempt_2"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 279, "key": "FACT-0398: A learned contextual parent ranker BEATS the deployed argmax decisively on fold 1 and FAILS to transfer to fold 0 - LEVER-0041's falsifier (e) fires. ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "A learned contextual parent ranker BEATS the deployed argmax decisively on fold 1 and FAILS to transfer to fold 0 - LEVER-0041's falsifier (e) fires. On the complete widened fold-1 surface, out-of-fold and crop-grouped, the bidirectional tree reaches contested top-1 0.762227 against the deployed 0.708394, a gain of +0.053833 with 2,316 gained against 884 lost for net +1,432 and a paired interval of [+0.04687, +0.06150] that excludes zero favourably. The ladder is monotone in representation - linear +0.0273, tree +0.0418, bidirectional +0.0538 - and the noise floor MEASURED ON THIS SURFACE is NEGATIVE at -0.001391, so none of the gain is quantile binning. Frozen and applied unchanged to fold 0 it scores 0.817176, a delta of -0.016599 whose interval [-0.02699, -0.00586] excludes zero ON THE WRONG SIDE: negative transfer, not merely absent", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold-1 surface, out-of-fold only, crop-grouped, with the model FROZEN by sha256 on fold 1 before fold 0 was touched - so gate B measures transfer rather than fit. The noise floor was measured on THIS surface rather than inherited from FACT-0386, and its paired instrument check passed exactly: a linear model on the probability alone reproduces the deployed contested top-1 to all sixteen digits with churn zero, and the instrument refuses to report if it does not.", "value": "-0.016599 frozen_fold1_model_contested_top1_delta_on_fold0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 280, "key": "FACT-0399: Gate 1 attempt 3 carried a LIVE RECURRENCE of FACT-0387 and was stopped on CPU before it consumed a third GPU session. Fixing the dataset mount root l", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "Gate 1 attempt 3 carried a LIVE RECURRENCE of FACT-0387 and was stopped on CPU before it consumed a third GPU session. Fixing the dataset mount root left the import boundary broken: the worker launcher passed no env, so PYTHONPATH was unset, and the worker's own comment asserted it would \"resolve because cwd is the repo root\" - which is false, because sys.path[0] is the SCRIPT's directory (/kaggle/working), not the working directory. Executed rather than read, three ways: as built it raises ModuleNotFoundError; with the deployed shards' own PYTHONPATH=src it STILL raises, because predict_unet_transformer lives in scripts/ and not src/; only scripts+src resolves it", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Established by EXECUTION on CPU - the worker was lifted verbatim from the built notebook, the Kaggle layout was mirrored, and it was launched the way the notebook launches it - not by reading the source. Two independent instruments agreed: an auditor's reproduction and the preflight's PF07.", "value": "3 consecutive_gate1_attempts_carrying_an_import_or_path_defect"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 281, "key": "FACT-0400: The Gate 1 worker does not reproduce the deployed IMAGE PIPELINE, and this is a silent defect that would have made the gate measure its own preprocess", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The Gate 1 worker does not reproduce the deployed IMAGE PIPELINE, and this is a silent defect that would have made the gate measure its own preprocessing rather than the cache. The deployed predict_video opens the dataset with normalize=False and load_image=False, reads the zarr group \"0\" directly, and normalises using the dataset's own recorded quantiles 0.001 and 0.999 - raising if they are absent - while carrying downsample (1, 4, 4) into both the array and the voxel size. The Gate 1 worker instead calls open_dataset(path).image with NO arguments, taking normalize=True by default and no downsample at all, so it feeds the trunk a differently normalised image at a different spatial resolution. Combined with the four defects already found, five separate faults have been identified in three attempts at this gate", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read at named lines in the deployed predictor and in the io module's signature, and compared against the worker's own call. The normalisation difference is not a matter of degree: the deployed path explicitly disables open_dataset's normalisation and substitutes a quantile scheme of its own, so the two paths cannot agree by coincidence. The downsample difference changes the spatial resolution the trunk sees, which changes every feature it produces.", "value": "5 distinct_defects_found_in_the_gate_1_worker"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 282, "key": "FACT-0401: The P35 exploitation treatment is PREREGISTERED at a central of 0.931, band 0.927 to 0.935, with the falsifier at a score AT OR BELOW 0.931 - and the ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The P35 exploitation treatment is PREREGISTERED at a central of 0.931, band 0.927 to 0.935, with the falsifier at a score AT OR BELOW 0.931 - and the central estimate therefore SITS ON the falsifier, which is deliberate. The kernel is COMPLETE and the treatment is confirmed live in its own log: the run loaded best.pt at epoch 2 rather than skipping it, ran with the safe-division veto ON, and deepcenter_rejected is NON-ZERO across movies (11, 36, 0, 67, 3, 29, 1, 27) where the released 0.931 base recorded exactly zero on all eight. The detector now decides; on the base it decided nothing", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The BAND is a stated prior and not a measurement - this configuration cannot be validated offline at all because its secondary saw all 199 movies (FACT-0378), so nothing here predicts the score. What is VERIFIED is the preregistration itself and the treatment's effect: the prereg file was hashed at 09:19:17Z with \"no treatment built yet\" recorded beside it, an hour before the build, and the per-movie deepcenter_rejected counts are read from the run's own fetched log.", "value": "0.931 preregistered_central_for_the_p35_dcveto_exchange"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 283, "key": "FACT-0402: A trunk node feature is WINDOW-DEPENDENT, so a frame-keyed feature cache is scientifically undefined and every previous Gate 1 design was measuring th", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "A trunk node feature is WINDOW-DEPENDENT, so a frame-keyed feature cache is scientifically undefined and every previous Gate 1 design was measuring the wrong object. TemporalUNet3D contains _TemporalAttention, which mixes across the window's time axis, so unet_out[:, i] depends on EVERY frame in the window. At the deployed window_size 2 with stride W-1 = 1, an interior frame t is the TARGET of the pair (t-1, t) from window [t-1, t] and the SOURCE of the pair (t, t+1) from window [t, t+1] - two different forward passes and two different feature vectors for the same node. Measured on the real deployed path, 66 of 173 role-nodes carry two vectors, with a maximum absolute delta of 0.0123 and a maximum relative delta of 3.5%, median relative 1.0% - 2.1 ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE above the gate's own 1e-4 tolerance. The error is not uniform across the source axis, so the documented blind spot would NOT have hidden it", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured on the real deployed path with the real class rather than read from source or inferred from a stub - which matters here, because the previous suite's stub could not have exhibited window mixing at all. The delta is two orders of magnitude above the tolerance the gate itself declares, so this is not a marginal effect that a looser bound would absorb.", "value": "0.0123 max_abs_feature_delta_between_a_nodes_source_role_and_target_role_vectors"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 284, "key": "FACT-0403: Gate 1 attempt 4 (P36, the passive tap) RAN AND MEASURED for the first time in four attempts. It is NOT a failed cache: passivity is PROVEN, the pair-", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "Gate 1 attempt 4 (P36, the passive tap) RAN AND MEASURED for the first time in four attempts. It is NOT a failed cache: passivity is PROVEN, the pair-and-role schema is PROVEN, structural integrity is PROVEN, and the parity verdict is INVALID rather than negative - because the reference quantity it compared against was downstream of secondary fusion. The tap captured both expected crops with real deployed quantities - feat_dim 32, pos_dim 32, downsample (1,4,4), real per-crop quantiles - passivity verified both statically and in-kernel, integrity failures ZERO, positional features round-tripping EXACTLY at 0.0, and both probability bands non-vacuous on both crops (band A 1,703 and 2,496 checked; band B 998 and 8,909). The replay nevertheless disagrees by up to 0.43 because THE COMPARISON TARGET IS WRONG: the deployed probs are computed AFTER a secondary-model logit blend at weight 0.15, while the replay re-runs the PRIMARY HEAD ONLY from cache", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Diagnosed from the run's own fetched log and the deployed source at named lines, without opening the archived cache and without modifying anything - the host's instruction after a gate failure is to persist and reproduce offline before touching the mechanism. The attribution is not inferred from the magnitude: the log records \"Secondary edge-logit weight: 0.15\" and the deployed source computes probs from the blended logits, so the reference the tap recorded is by construction a two-model quantity.", "value": "0.4286353588104248 max_abs_prob_delta_between_primary_only_replay_and_blended_deployed_probs"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 285, "key": "FACT-0404: The public 0.933 notebook differs from our released 0.931 champion by EXACTLY TWO ENVIRONMENT VALUES and nothing else. Cell-by-cell over all ten cells", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The public 0.933 notebook differs from our released 0.931 champion by EXACTLY TWO ENVIRONMENT VALUES and nothing else. Cell-by-cell over all ten cells, the only substantive differences are BIOHUB_BIDIRECTIONAL_EDGE_WEIGHT 0.15 -> 0.30 and BIOHUB_SECONDARY_DETECTION_WEIGHT 0.475 -> 0.80, each appearing twice because both are re-asserted in a guard block that the notebook checks against itself. No code, no model, no threshold, no candidate rule and no post-processing differs. The author's own comment states the single change against THEIR fork was the detection weight, which places the bidirectional 0.30 in the fork they started from rather than in their contribution", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The DIFF is verified - it is a cell-by-cell comparison of two notebooks on disk and it is exact. What is SUSPECT is any causal reading of the 0.933. It is an EXTERNAL leaderboard number on someone else's account, unreproduced by us, and two knobs moved together, so neither is attributable on this evidence. The author's claimed +0.003 for the detection weight is measured on THEIR lineage, not ours, and we have no control arm for it.", "value": "2 environment_values_separating_the_public_0933_from_our_0931"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 286, "key": "FACT-0405: DEFECT 7, and it is the same signature as five of the six before it. The training harness's own structural gate compared cached coordinates to the pre", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "DEFECT 7, and it is the same signature as five of the six before it. The training harness's own structural gate compared cached coordinates to the pre-ILP export RAW, but the tap flushes BEFORE the deployed rescale - predict_unet_transformer.py:798-802 multiplies coords[:, 1:] by the downsample factor after the concatenate - so the cache holds the DOWNSAMPLED grid while the export records the original resolution. At the deployed downsample (1,4,4) the check rejects EVERY real cache. It passed only because its fixture used downsample (1,1,1), where the rescale is the identity. Calibrated against the real P36 artifact: WITH the rescale, zero parity failures across all 26,169 and 33,432 nodes of both crops; WITHOUT it, failure on both", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read at the named deployed lines and then CALIBRATED against the real archived P36 cache in both directions - with the rescale it passes on every node of both crops, without it it fails on both. A one-directional check would not have distinguished a correct rescale from a vacuous comparison.", "value": "7 distinct_defects_found_in_the_gate_1_and_cache_lineage"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 287, "key": "FACT-0406: At FULL capture on real 32-dimensional features, window dependence is an order of magnitude larger than the smoke measurement suggested: 1,539 of 3,52", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "At FULL capture on real 32-dimensional features, window dependence is an order of magnitude larger than the smoke measurement suggested: 1,539 of 3,521 role-nodes on one P36 crop and 2,786 of 6,465 on the other carry two distinct feature vectors, with maximum absolute deltas of 0.3001 and 0.8958. This must NOT be conflated with FACT-0402's 0.0123, which was measured over 66 of 173 role-nodes under a different normalisation on the CPU smoke trunk", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured on the real archived P36 cache through the migrated harness's own role index, with every recorded band edge resolving through that index (2,701 and 11,405) - so the dual-role population is counted over the same edges the head was actually fed, not over a synthetic surface.", "value": "0.8958 max_abs_role_feature_delta_at_full_capture_p36"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 288, "key": "FACT-0407: THE P36 CACHE WAS FAITHFUL AND WOULD HAVE PASSED A CORRECTLY-TARGETED GATE. Re-derived on CPU from P36's own archived cache: a primary-only replay rep", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE P36 CACHE WAS FAITHFUL AND WOULD HAVE PASSED A CORRECTLY-TARGETED GATE. Re-derived on CPU from P36's own archived cache: a primary-only replay reproduces the GPU verdict to seven digits - band-A max delta 0.22877353 against the recorded 0.22877401, and 0.42863509 against 0.42863536 - and applying the BIDIRECTIONAL HARMONIC at weight 0.20 collapses it to 6.56e-07 and 1.13e-06, with band-A membership going from 12 missing / 0 extra and 109 / 39 to ZERO on both crops. That is inside the gate's own 1e-4 tolerance by two orders of magnitude. The secondary model was DISABLED in this run, not active at 0.15 as FACT-0403 first recorded", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Computed on CPU from the archived P36 cache and the real pack weights located by sha256, not inferred. The primary-only arm REPRODUCES the GPU verdict to seven significant digits, which is what makes the second arm interpretable: the same code path that recovers the known-wrong number also recovers the right one when the fusion is applied. The predictor used was verified byte-identical to the source the tap patched.", "value": "1.1324882507324219e-06 max_abs_band_a_delta_after_reproducing_the_deployed_bidirectional_fusion"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 289, "key": "FACT-0408: DEFECT 8. The Gate-1 CPU suite was testing the WRONG PROGRAM. It built its sandbox from vendor/kaggle-cell-tracking - the organizer's public repositor", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "DEFECT 8. The Gate-1 CPU suite was testing the WRONG PROGRAM. It built its sandbox from vendor/kaggle-cell-tracking - the organizer's public repository - while the kernel materialises the support pack into /kaggle/working/tracking_repo and runs that. The vendored predictor is 677 lines with ZERO occurrences of \"secondary\"; the deployed one is 1047 lines and contains BOTH fusion stages. A green suite was therefore structurally incapable of catching any fusion defect, including the one that invalidated P36's verdict", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Both files were read and counted. The distinction is not stylistic: a 677-line predictor with no secondary code cannot exhibit a fusion defect at all, so every test in that suite was passing on a program that could not fail the way the real one did.", "value": "0 occurrences_of_secondary_in_the_vendored_predictor_the_suite_tested"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 290, "key": "FACT-0409: The feature-cache contract moved from 1 to 2 by a delta VERIFIED by ast-diff rather than by hand: 52 keys to 79, exactly THREE removed and THIRTY adde", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The feature-cache contract moved from 1 to 2 by a delta VERIFIED by ast-diff rather than by hand: 52 keys to 79, exactly THREE removed and THIRTY added. The three removed are the unqualified probability fields band_a_prob, band_b_prob and edge_prob - no field named merely \"probability\" survives. Two further contracts the migration brief did not name were found by reading the tap and locked as well: the per-band selection surface, where bands A and B are selected on deployed_probs_postblend while band P is selected on primary_probs_preblend, and the contract version itself. The drift lock is exact set equality in BOTH directions, so a new key on either side fails on CPU", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The delta was computed by ast-parsing the tap's own _AFT_SCHEMA_REQUIRED and set-differencing against the auditor's list, not by transcribing a brief - and the brief turned out to be correct in every entry, which is only knowable because it was checked. The no-fusion identity is measured on the real deployed predictor in both directions: exactly 0.0 with no stage, 0.313 with a secondary at 0.15, so the conditions that rest on it are not vacuous.", "value": "79 required_cache_keys_under_contract_2"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 291, "key": "FACT-0410: The archived P36 cache is CONTRACT 1 and is now rejected for training under the named condition cache_contract_1. It keeps its full EVIDENTIARY value ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The archived P36 cache is CONTRACT 1 and is now rejected for training under the named condition cache_contract_1. It keeps its full EVIDENTIARY value - it is the artifact FACT-0403, FACT-0406 and FACT-0407 were measured on - and loses only its LICENCE value. No legacy read-only mode is admitted, because contract 1 stored ONE probability column and the pre-fusion surface it never held cannot be recovered by any rewrite of those bytes", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The rejection was observed on both crops of the real archived artifact, and the reasoning against a legacy mode is not a preference: FACT-0407 recovered the pre-fusion surface by RE-RUNNING the primary head against real pack weights, not by reading the cache, which demonstrates directly that the information is absent from those bytes.", "value": "1 contract_version_of_the_archived_p36_cache"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 292, "key": "FACT-0411: Contract 2 leaves ZERO usable feature caches on disk. Every contract-2 cache in existence is a CPU smoke fixture at feature dimension 8; the only depl", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "Contract 2 leaves ZERO usable feature caches on disk. Every contract-2 cache in existence is a CPU smoke fixture at feature dimension 8; the only deployed-scale artifact, P36's archive, is contract 1 and is now refused under the named condition cache_contract_1 rather than the generic cache_schema_incomplete. Three harness tests that used it as a schema fixture were RETIRED rather than accommodated, and replaced by one asserting the opposite - that both archived crops are refused, with the condition name preserved and a freshly built contract-2 world as the accept control", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The refusal was observed on both archived crops through the harness's own entry points, and the distinction between the two condition names was asserted rather than assumed - thirty missing keys reported as cache_schema_incomplete would send an operator hunting a truncated write instead of a contract change.", "value": "0 deployed_scale_contract_2_caches_available"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "low", "id": 293, "key": "FACT-0412: The P35 DeepCenter/veto exchange scored 0.932, clearing its falsifier by the SMALLEST DISTINGUISHABLE MARGIN. The preregistered central was 0.931 with", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "The P35 DeepCenter/veto exchange scored 0.932, clearing its falsifier by the SMALLEST DISTINGUISHABLE MARGIN. The preregistered central was 0.931 with a band of 0.927 to 0.935 and a falsifier at or below 0.931; 0.932 is +0.001 on the base and did not fire it. The claim is therefore confirmed and the confirmation is weak: the packet's own reasoning (h), written before the run, states that public-LB variance alone is of the order of the effect under test, so a single +0.001 submission cannot separate a real component gain from leaderboard noise. LEVER-0042 closes and the lane ENDS, as preregistered, whatever the score", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "The SCORE is the competition's own number and is not in doubt. What is SUSPECT is the ATTRIBUTION of +0.001 to the component: one submission at the resolution of the leaderboard's own variance cannot distinguish a real effect from noise, and the packet said so before the run rather than after. The falsifier was a hard threshold and it did not fire - that is the honest reading, and it is weaker than \"the component works\".", "value": "0.932 public_lb_score_of_the_deepcenter_veto_exchange_on_the_0931_base"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 294, "key": "FACT-0413: ON THE DISCOVERY FOLD A CONTEXTUAL PARENT SCORER BEATS THE DEPLOYED ARGMAX, AND THE GAIN IS NOT BINNING. On the complete widened P34 fold-1 surface - ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "ON THE DISCOVERY FOLD A CONTEXTUAL PARENT SCORER BEATS THE DEPLOYED ARGMAX, AND THE GAIN IS NOT BINNING. On the complete widened P34 fold-1 surface - all 128 crops, all 91,410 decidable targets, crop-grouped 5-fold, out-of-fold only - six of seven preregistered arms beat the deployed contested top-1 of FACT-0388 with a crop-paired ci95 excluding zero on the favourable side. The best arm A4.bidir.tree reaches contested top-1 0.762227, delta +0.053833, gained 2,316 / lost 884 / net +1,432 with churn 3,200 and ci95 [+0.046868, +0.061500]. The ladder is monotone in REPRESENTATION rather than in head class - linear +0.027330 < tree +0.041841 < bidirectional +0.053833 - which is the direction FACT-0386 predicted when it found the head was not the constraint. The binning floor was MEASURED on this surface rather than inherited and it is NEGATIVE: a tree given only the deployed probability posts delta -0.001391, net -37, churn 315, so no part of +0.053833 is the quantile-binning artifact that halved FACT-0386's fold-0 arm", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete fold 1, all 128 crops, out-of-fold only, splits GROUPED BY CROP so no target contributes to its own training fold, on a surface whose sha256 is recorded in the payload and which was materialised out of PKT-0036's audit scratch into the acquisition's own directory and verified byte-identical before use. The harness carries its own internal control and REFUSES rather than reports if it fails: a linear model on the probability alone returns the deployed contested top-1 to all sixteen digits with churn 0, which is the only arithmetically possible outcome for a correct protocol. The run was repeated end to end after two module-identity defects were fixed and both runs agree bit-for-bit on every arm's top-1, gained/lost/net/churn, interval and calibration, differing only by two 1-ulp float-summation drifts in a descriptive margin mean. WHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH is stated in the note and is large.", "value": "0.05383256268561332 contested_parent_top1_delta_over_deployed_f1_widened_oof"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 295, "key": "FACT-0414: THE FOLD-0 GATE REFUSED THE FOLD-1 WINNER TWICE, AND THE TWO REFUSALS DISAGREE IN A WAY NEITHER READING EXPLAINS. LEVER-0041 falsifier (e) fires as wr", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE FOLD-0 GATE REFUSED THE FOLD-1 WINNER TWICE, AND THE TWO REFUSALS DISAGREE IN A WAY NEITHER READING EXPLAINS. LEVER-0041 falsifier (e) fires as written. GATE_B, weight transfer with the fold-1 fit applied and NO fold-0 fitting of any kind, returns contested top-1 0.817176, delta -0.016599, gained 133 / lost 202 / net -69, ci95 [-0.026989, -0.005860] - an interval EXCLUDING ZERO ON THE WRONG SIDE, which is negative transfer and strictly stronger than no transfer. GATE_A, architecture transfer with the IDENTICAL recipe refitted out of fold on fold 0's own crop-grouped splits so no cross-checkpoint difference can exist, returns contested top-1 0.8337743565070964 - the deployed value to all sixteen digits - with delta EXACTLY 0.000000, gained 36 / lost 36, churn 72, ci95 [-0.003546, +0.003465]. It genuinely reshuffled 72 targets and netted precisely nothing", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Both arms ran on the complete fold-0 widened surface, all 71 crops, out-of-fold, crop-grouped, through the SAME committed harness that produced FACT-0413 and FACT-0386, so the three are directly comparable rather than merely adjacent. The freeze is mechanical rather than declared: the fold-1 winner was pickled and sha256-pinned before fold 0 was read, and the transfer head's `fit` CANNOT modify the model: it increments a counter and returns self without touching `model_` (scripts/win_bet/assoc_tournament.py:480-482), while the constructor re-hashes the pickle and REFUSES if the bytes moved since the freeze was recorded (:471-476). GATE_A removes the checkpoint difference entirely by refitting, which is what makes the pair interpretable at all. CORRECTED 2026-08-30 by the PKT-0036 audit: an earlier draft of this reason claimed a silent refit \"would be visible in the payload\". That was FALSE and is not how the freeze is enforced - `n_fit_calls_` is incremented and read by NOTHING, serialised into no payload and asserted in no test, so the counter is decorative. The guarantee is structural rather than observational, which is stronger, but the claim as first written was unsupported and would have sent a reader to a payload key that does not exist.", "value": "0.0 gate_a_refit_contested_parent_top1_delta_f0_widened_oof"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 296, "key": "FACT-0415: TWO INDEPENDENTLY-SEEDED HEADS OF OUR OWN MAKE ALMOST THE SAME ERRORS, SO THE CONSENSUS ROUTE IS DIVERSITY-LIMITED RATHER THAN RULE-LIMITED. An altern", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "TWO INDEPENDENTLY-SEEDED HEADS OF OUR OWN MAKE ALMOST THE SAME ERRORS, SO THE CONSENSUS ROUTE IS DIVERSITY-LIMITED RATHER THAN RULE-LIMITED. An alternate-seed secondary - different seed, 0.7 row bootstrap - lands at contested top-1 0.762189 against the primary's 0.762227 and the two agree on 97.95% of the 26,601 contested fold-1 targets: both correct 20,003, both wrong 6,053, primary-only 273, secondary-only 272. The oracle of the two reaches 0.772452, so a PERFECT consensus rule could buy at most +0.010 over the primary, and top-1 where they agree is 0.767693 against 0.762227 pooled - making agreement a usable abstention trigger but a weak one", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Computed over the complete contested fold-1 population through the same committed harness, with both heads fitted out of fold on the same crop-grouped splits, so the agreement rate is not inflated by one head having seen targets the other had not.", "value": "0.9795120484192323 contested_target_agreement_rate_between_two_independently_seeded_heads_f1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 297, "key": "FACT-0416: Contract-2 worst-case cache storage is 1,580 BYTES PER DETECTED NODE, re-derived from the tap's own declared dtypes in the built notebook rather than ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "Contract-2 worst-case cache storage is 1,580 BYTES PER DETECTED NODE, re-derived from the tap's own declared dtypes in the built notebook rather than inherited - role row 302 B at feat_dim 32 and pos_dim 32 bounded at 2 rows per node, band row 64 B at 10 rows, union row 24 B at 9 rows, node-side 120 B - and independently reproduced by the auditor's own constant. Full fold, uncompressed: fold 0 at 2,332,346 nodes needs 3.43 GiB single trunk and 6.86 GiB dual; fold 1 at 2,523,479 nodes needs 3.71 and 7.43 GiB. THIS SUPERSEDES PKT-0037's EARLIER 0.61/0.66 GB DUAL-TRUNK ESTIMATE, which assumed 128 B/node and was 12.3x LOW", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Computed from the dtypes the built notebook itself declares, not from a design document, and reproduced independently by a second instrument that arrived at the same constant. The fold-0 node table was tied to P36's own recorded per-crop counts before being used, which is what distinguishes it from the pre-ILP table that would have understated the requirement by about 15%.", "value": "1580 worst_case_contract_2_cache_bytes_per_detected_node"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 298, "key": "FACT-0417: FIVE MORE DEFECTS, ALL IN THE LAUNCH-PREFLIGHT INSTRUMENT ITSELF AND ALL CAUGHT ON CPU, taking the running ledger of this lineage from eight to THIRTE", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "FIVE MORE DEFECTS, ALL IN THE LAUNCH-PREFLIGHT INSTRUMENT ITSELF AND ALL CAUGHT ON CPU, taking the running ledger of this lineage from eight to THIRTEEN: a hardcoded contract-1 band-field list; a floor detector matching a literal expression form rather than the behaviour; stale mutation-test names; the signed RECEIPT's expected_gpu_outputs hardcoded to the contract-1 parity worker; and input_hashes keyed on the string \"None\". Each produced a FALSE FAIL or a FALSE PASS against a CORRECT contract-2 notebook. The receipt defect is the most dangerous of the five because the POST-RUN AUDIT READS THAT FILE and nobody re-derives it - a correct tap run would have been failed, and a tap that recorded nothing would have passed unnoticed", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Each defect is pinned by a MUTATION that fails without the fix rather than by an assertion that it is gone, and all five were found against the real contract-2 artifact rather than a fixture. The receipt defect was demonstrated in BOTH directions - a correct run failing and an empty run passing - which is what establishes it as a false-pass hazard and not only a false-fail nuisance.", "value": "13 cumulative_distinct_defects_in_the_gate_1_cache_and_launch_lineage"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 299, "key": "FACT-0418: NO DECLARED DUAL-TRUNK PAIR HAS A FOLD-LEGITIMATE ARM ON EITHER FOLD. Every dual_trunk_pair in scripts/win_bet/assoc_specs/ is ['official','stabledet'", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "NO DECLARED DUAL-TRUNK PAIR HAS A FOLD-LEGITIMATE ARM ON EITHER FOLD. Every dual_trunk_pair in scripts/win_bet/assoc_specs/ is ['official','stabledet'] and both roles are marked fold_legitimate false on BOTH folds, while the only legitimate trunks - pack_split0 on fold 0 and our own OOF split_1 on fold 1 - appear in no declared pair. Worse, audit_feature_cache.PKT0029_REQUIRED_TRUNK_ROLES is ('official','stabledet'), so the audit would REFUSE the honest pair and ACCEPT the pair with no legitimate arm. Separately, the 'official' role's provenance is RETRACTED to UNVERIFIED: C:/temp/hoct/trunks/official_f0/edge_predictor_best.pth is BYTE-IDENTICAL (sha256 d3e89eb361eeadef) to our own OOF split_0, not the HOCT publisher default it was recorded as", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Established by HASHING THE BYTES rather than reading the documented role, which is precisely how the retraction arose - the earlier record asserted the publisher's documented provenance for a file that is byte-identical to one of our own checkpoints. The located fold-1 trunk was verified in two places, on disk and as an attached Kaggle dataset, and its resolver was read at named lines.", "value": "0 declared_dual_trunk_pairs_with_a_fold_legitimate_arm_on_either_fold"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 300, "key": "FACT-0419: THE FOLD-1 ASSOCIATION GAIN IS NOT A SELECTION ARTIFACT, AND PKT-0038's FALSIFIER (g) DOES NOT FIRE. The 2x2 train/test matrix is complete and the pre", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE FOLD-1 ASSOCIATION GAIN IS NOT A SELECTION ARTIFACT, AND PKT-0038's FALSIFIER (g) DOES NOT FIRE. The 2x2 train/test matrix is complete and the previously missing cell WINS: a head fitted on fold 0 - never selected on anything, never having seen a fold-1 crop, embryo or edge-predictor checkpoint - beats the deployed argmax on fold-1 contested targets by +0.006616, gained 473 / lost 297, with a crop-paired ci95 of [+0.00443, +0.00876] that EXCLUDES ZERO FAVOURABLY. Selection on the discovery fold cannot explain a gain produced by a model that was never selected", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The three known cells were ASSERTED against FACT-0413 and FACT-0414 and all three checks passed BEFORE the fourth cell was computed, so the new number was produced by a pipeline already demonstrated to reproduce the registry rather than by one tuned until it did. The new cell is crop-grouped out-of-fold like the other three, and its head saw no fold-1 data of any kind.", "value": "0.006616292620578168 contested_parent_top1_delta_of_a_fold0_fitted_head_evaluated_on_fold_1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 301, "key": "FACT-0420: GATE A's EXACT ZERO IS THE OUT-OF-FOLD COLLAPSE OF A WHOLLY OPTIMISTIC IN-SAMPLE SIGNAL, AND IT IS LOCALISED NOTHING RATHER THAN CANCELLATION OR UNIFO", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "GATE A's EXACT ZERO IS THE OUT-OF-FOLD COLLAPSE OF A WHOLLY OPTIMISTIC IN-SAMPLE SIGNAL, AND IT IS LOCALISED NOTHING RATHER THAN CANCELLATION OR UNIFORM NOTHING. Measured at the ARGMAX rather than at correctness - churn is blind to wrong-for-wrong swaps - the fold-0 refit picks a different parent on only 81 of 4,157 contested targets, ALL 81 in the LOWEST primary-margin quartile, with agreement EXACTLY 1.0000 on the other 3,118; of the 81, 36 gained, 36 lost and 9 were wrong-for-wrong. The apparent-versus-out-of-fold ceiling explains the null directly: fold 0 goes from an apparent +0.024056 to an out-of-fold +0.000000, so ZERO PER CENT of the in-sample signal survives, while fold 1 goes from +0.065975 to +0.053833 and 81.6% survives. Fold 0 carries about ten contested errors per crop", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured at the ARGMAX rather than at correctness, which is the distinction that makes the finding possible at all: gained/lost/churn cannot see a swap from one wrong parent to another, and 9 of the 81 changed targets are exactly that. The strata are the preregistered ones and the quartile concentration is a property of the data rather than a chosen cut.", "value": "0.0 share_of_the_apparent_fold0_contested_gain_surviving_out_of_fold"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 302, "key": "FACT-0421: THE RAW DEPLOYED PROBABILITY IS THE NON-TRANSFERRING COMPONENT, AND REMOVING IT MAKES THE SCORER TRANSFER IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Deleting the raw probabi", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE RAW DEPLOYED PROBABILITY IS THE NON-TRANSFERRING COMPONENT, AND REMOVING IT MAKES THE SCORER TRANSFER IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Deleting the raw probability column swings the frozen transfer arm by +0.0197: the full recipe transfers fold 1 to fold 0 at -0.016599, while the PROBABILITY-FREE CONTEXTUAL recipe transfers at +0.003127 fold 1 to fold 0 and +0.001842 fold 0 to fold 1, favourable. Louder still, pure GEOMETRY beats the deployed argmax on fold 1 by +0.045788 out of fold while LOSING 0.031032 on fold 0 - so the deployed `prob` carries different SKILL on the two folds, which is a property of the feature and not of any head fitted on it", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The ablations run on the same crop-grouped out-of-fold protocol and the same data contract as the arms they are compared against, so the swing is attributable to the deleted column rather than to a protocol difference. Two independent reconciliations with FACT-0386 landed EXACTLY on the first run - the binning floor's gained/lost/net/churn and the geometry-alone figure - which is what licenses reading the new ablations as commensurable with that earlier work.", "value": "0.0197 swing_in_the_frozen_fold1_to_fold0_transfer_from_deleting_the_raw_probability_column"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 303, "key": "FACT-0422: THE UNIFIED LOST-EDGE LEDGER PUTS THE PARENT-RESCORING PRIZE FAR BELOW THE NEVER-OFFERED PRIZE ON BOTH FOLDS. Attributing every recoverable miss to th", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE UNIFIED LOST-EDGE LEDGER PUTS THE PARENT-RESCORING PRIZE FAR BELOW THE NEVER-OFFERED PRIZE ON BOTH FOLDS. Attributing every recoverable miss to the stage responsible, in six mutually exclusive first-match-wins categories, through the official matcher, with exhaustiveness ASSERTED rather than reported: fold 0 of 19,826 GT edges gives endpoint-absent 161, endpoint-removed 198, NEVER-OFFERED 1,110, WRONG-PARENT 240, overwritten-downstream 73 (provisional), division-topology 0, recovered 18,044; fold 1 of 109,057 gives 11,001 / 5,717 / NEVER-OFFERED 14,007 / WRONG-PARENT 1,735 / overwritten 537 (provisional) / 0 / recovered 76,060. Never-offered exceeds wrong-parent by 4.6x on fold 0 and 8.1x on fold 1", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The six categories are ordered and first-match-wins, so no lost edge is counted twice, and the instrument ASSERTS closure - the six counts plus recovered edges must sum to the GT total - rather than reporting it. The assertion was exercised by the auditor against dropped mass, double-counted mass and category 6 absorbing category 4. Reconciliation with FACT-0370, FACT-0376, FACT-0371 and FACT-0080 held on the FIRST run, which is the strongest available evidence that the partition is the same one the earlier facts measured.", "value": "240 fold0_gt_edges_lost_to_wrong_parent_selection_the_entire_parent_rescoring_prize"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 304, "key": "FACT-0423: FOCUS-3D IS ADMISSIBLE UNDER THE COMPETITION'S OWN RULE TEXT, AND THREE LICENCES BIND AN INTEGRATION RATHER THAN THE TWO ADVERTISED. Rule 2.6.b states", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "FOCUS-3D IS ADMISSIBLE UNDER THE COMPETITION'S OWN RULE TEXT, AND THREE LICENCES BIND AN INTEGRATION RATHER THAN THE TWO ADVERTISED. Rule 2.6.b states that external data and models are acceptable unless specifically prohibited by the Host, subject to being reasonably accessible to all and of minimal cost; no Host prohibition exists, and the Reasonableness Standard is about EXCESSIVE COST excluding participants, its worked example being a licence costing more than the prize - which a free auto-approved gate is not. Rule 2.5.a.3 is stronger still and is incoherent unless pretrained models are permitted. The licences are BSD-3-Clause code, a SEPARATE MIT Copyright (c) 2022 Meta, Inc. inside src/focus3d/segmentation/FOCUS3D/ from the Mask2Former lineage which the top-level badge hides, and Apache-2.0 weights asserted in ONE README SENTENCE with no LICENSE file and no card metadata", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The admissibility verdict rests on QUOTED rule text whose provenance was authenticated against an independent RPC payload before it was relied on, rather than on a summary of the rules. The third licence was found by reading the source tree rather than the advertised badge, which is the only way it could have been found. What remains weak is stated rather than smoothed over: the weights grant is one README sentence with no LICENSE artifact - a real grant from the rights holder, but a thin one.", "value": "3 distinct_licences_binding_a_focus3d_integration"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 305, "key": "FACT-0424: NO OVERLAP WAS FOUND BETWEEN FOCUS-3D's PUBLISHED DATA INVENTORY AND THIS COMPETITION's SOURCES, SO LEVER-0043 IS NOT RESTRICTED TO SUBMISSION-ONLY JU", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "NO OVERLAP WAS FOUND BETWEEN FOCUS-3D's PUBLISHED DATA INVENTORY AND THIS COMPETITION's SOURCES, SO LEVER-0043 IS NOT RESTRICTED TO SUBMISSION-ONLY JUDGEMENT. The only published inventory is the project's dataset portal - 14 families, 82 volumes, 400,000+ instances, sourced to the Schier lab, Keller lab, Hufnagel group, Cell Tracking Challenge, Allen Institute and their own collection. CZI Biohub, Zebrahub and the Royer lab appear NOWHERE, and no listed volume carries our z-ratio of 4.0 (theirs are 5, 5.86 and 8). The FACT-0378 trap therefore does not fire and offline evaluation of these embeddings stays interpretable", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "THIS IS NEGATIVE EVIDENCE FROM A SOURCE THAT IS NOT A TRAINING MANIFEST, and it is labelled accordingly rather than promoted. The portal is a \"gold-standard datasets\" listing, not a stated train/test split, and there is no paper. Absence from a curated showcase is not proof of absence from a training set. The verdict is \"no overlap found\", which is weaker than \"no overlap exists\", and it must be quoted in that form.", "value": "0 overlapping_data_sources_found_between_focus3d_and_this_competition"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 306, "key": "FACT-0425: THE NAMED PACKAGING BLOCKER FOR FOCUS-3D IS DEAD, AND IT WAS KILLED BY RUNNING THE GRAPH RATHER THAN BY READING IT. The upstream repository does ship ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE NAMED PACKAGING BLOCKER FOR FOCUS-3D IS DEAD, AND IT WAS KILLED BY RUNNING THE GRAPH RATHER THAN BY READING IT. The upstream repository does ship a compiled CUDA op, so the risk was genuine, but the publisher already solved it for inference: adapter_modules.py:134 defines MSDeformAttn3D_PyTorch on F.grid_sample at :285, instantiated at :447 and :513, and the packaged runtime ships no ops/ directory at all, grepping zero for every compiled-op marker. The complete 411.6M-parameter graph BUILDS AND FORWARDS END TO END ON CPU in this repository's own venv, returning pred_masks of shape [300, 32, 96, 96]. No bespoke T4 / CC 7.5 wheel is required and the requirement reduces to Kaggle's stock torch", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The blocker was retired by BUILDING AND FORWARDING the real graph on CPU, not by reading the source and inferring that the fallback would work - which matters because a source read cannot show that every instantiation path actually avoids the compiled op. The parameter count is separately and explicitly NOT verified: it was taken from an architecture instantiated with RANDOM weights and is numerically indistinguishable from a count off the released tensors, so its provenance ceiling is UNVERIFIED and the probe hard-codes that ceiling into its own output.", "value": "411638146 focus3d_parameters_in_the_instantiated_architecture_NOT_from_released_tensors"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 307, "key": "FACT-0426: IN THE DEPLOYED PROGRAM EXACTLY ONE OPERATION CAN CHANGE A TARGET'S ALREADY-ASSIGNED PARENT: motion_relink_edges, defined at built-notebook code line ", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "IN THE DEPLOYED PROGRAM EXACTLY ONE OPERATION CAN CHANGE A TARGET'S ALREADY-ASSIGNED PARENT: motion_relink_edges, defined at built-notebook code line 1823, deciding at 1890 via linear_sum_assignment, installed at 3073. Its body is BYTE-IDENTICAL (sha256_12 269758b0115d) across biohub-p3-harmonic, both P28 champion controls and P35. Every later edge-mutating stage is ADD-ONLY to targets with no incoming edge - close_single_frame_gaps, recover_strict_gap2, add_safe_divisions_postlink - or removes whole NODES rather than re-parenting them (prune_isolated, filter_short_track_components); the single-parent repair at 3077 is a MEASURED no-op with dropped_multi_parent_edges zero", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read at the cited deployed lines and then corroborated two ways rather than asserted: each stage's function BODY was hashed across four independently built notebooks and found identical, and the deployed chain's own counters in the replay evidence confirm the single-parent repair does nothing. The audit was performed against the 1047-line deployed support-pack predictor pinned by the repository's own test, never the vendored 677-line program that FACT-0408 records as a different program entirely.", "value": "1 deployed_operations_able_to_change_an_already_assigned_parent"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 308, "key": "FACT-0427: THE LEARNED ASSOCIATION SCORE REACHES THE FINAL PARENT SELECTION ONLY AS A BONUS BOUNDED BY 1.0, SUBTRACTED FROM A COST MEASURED IN MICROMETRES. At bu", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE LEARNED ASSOCIATION SCORE REACHES THE FINAL PARENT SELECTION ONLY AS A BONUS BOUNDED BY 1.0, SUBTRACTED FROM A COST MEASURED IN MICROMETRES. At built-notebook line 1889 the deployed cost is `cost[i, j] = motion + 0.05 * raw - MOTION_RELINK_LEARNED_BONUS * prob`, with the bonus deployed at 1.0 in every live env block and defaulting to 0.75. Its only input is learned_edge_probs, assembled at 3058-3069 from edge_prob on edges that SURVIVED THE ILP, so any pair the solver dropped scores exactly 0.0. edge_prob is the ONLY learned quantity that crosses the predictor subprocess boundary at all", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read at the cited deployed lines in the built notebook and the deployed predictor, with the bonus value confirmed in three separate live env blocks rather than inferred from the default. The claim that edge_prob is the only learned quantity crossing the boundary is a source read of the whole build_graph surface, not an absence argument from grep.", "value": "1.0 deployed_motion_relink_learned_bonus_the_entire_weight_of_the_learned_channel"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 309, "key": "FACT-0428: A CHANGE MADE ONLY AT PRE-ILP CANDIDATE RANKING IS MOSTLY DISCARDED BEFORE THE EMITTED GRAPH EXISTS, AND THE TWO FOLDS DIFFER BY ROUGHLY TWO-FOLD. For", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "A CHANGE MADE ONLY AT PRE-ILP CANDIDATE RANKING IS MOSTLY DISCARDED BEFORE THE EMITTED GRAPH EXISTS, AND THE TWO FOLDS DIFFER BY ROUGHLY TWO-FOLD. Forcing the sidecar runner-up as the parent and replaying the COMPLETE deployed chain: on fold 0, 3,056 of 3,613 forced choices whose target survived to emission are absent from the emitted graph - an overwrite rate of 0.8458 and a survival of 0.1542; on fold 1, 1,477 of 2,119, overwrite 0.6970 and survival 0.3030. The counterfactual on the SAME targets unperturbed is decisive about what this means: the pre-ILP parent IS the emitted parent for 4,092 of 4,198 fold-0 survivors (0.9747) and 2,401 of 2,529 fold-1 (0.9494). THE PIPELINE AGREES WITH ITS PRE-ILP RANKING; IT DOES NOT FOLLOW IT", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The control arm was asserted EXACT against the kernel's own run_stats across all fifteen compared columns before any perturbed arm was read, with a mismatch configured as a hard refusal - so the replay is demonstrated to reproduce the deployed chain rather than assumed to. The sample and its non-randomness are stated rather than smoothed over, and the direction of the resulting bias is named: these are a LOWER bound on what a well-aimed re-ranker would see.", "value": "0.1542 survival_rate_of_a_pre_ilp_only_parent_change_into_the_emitted_graph_fold0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 310, "key": "FACT-0429: SURVIVAL OF A FORCED PRE-ILP PARENT CHANGE FALLS MONOTONICALLY WITH THE PROMOTED PARENT'S GEOMETRIC HANDICAP, AND THE BREAK IS EXACTLY WHERE THE BONUS", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "SURVIVAL OF A FORCED PRE-ILP PARENT CHANGE FALLS MONOTONICALLY WITH THE PROMOTED PARENT'S GEOMETRIC HANDICAP, AND THE BREAK IS EXACTLY WHERE THE BONUS ARITHMETIC PREDICTS. Within 1.0 um of the deployed parent, survival is 104/185 = 0.5622 on fold 0 and 129/189 = 0.6825 on fold 1; outside it, 453/3,428 = 0.1321 and 513/1,930 = 0.2658 - ratios of 4.3x and 2.6x across precisely the boundary that a bonus of 1.0 against a micrometre-denominated cost implies. Only 5.1% of tested alternatives on fold 0 and 8.9% on fold 1 fall inside that band at all", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The boundary was PREDICTED from the deployed cost expression before it was measured, and the measured break lands there on both folds independently. That is a prediction meeting data rather than a cut chosen after inspecting the curve, which is what distinguishes this from a post-hoc threshold.", "value": "0.051 share_of_tested_alternative_parents_inside_the_band_where_the_learned_bonus_can_act_fold0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 311, "key": "FACT-0430: THE CATEGORY-2 DRAIN THAT MUST BE REMOVED FROM FACT-0370's REACHABLE SHARE BEFORE CATEGORY 4 IS COMPUTED: of every pre-ILP parent choice in the unpert", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE CATEGORY-2 DRAIN THAT MUST BE REMOVED FROM FACT-0370's REACHABLE SHARE BEFORE CATEGORY 4 IS COMPUTED: of every pre-ILP parent choice in the unperturbed control, 38,839 of 385,249 fold-0 targets (0.1008) and 22,729 of 165,735 fold-1 targets (0.1371) LOSE THEIR NODE before emission - to the ILP's node subset, to prune_isolated, or to the short-track filter. FACT-0370's \"endpoint detected\" pool is the PRE-ILP node set, upstream of all three of those operations, so that mass is inside its reachable share and outside the emitted graph", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured on the UNPERTURBED control arm of the same replay whose control was asserted exact against the kernel's own run_stats, so the drain is a property of the deployed chain rather than of the perturbation. The stage boundaries it attributes to were read at deployed file:line in FACT-0426 before the counting, so the three draining operations are named rather than inferred from a residual.", "value": "0.1008 share_of_pre_ilp_parent_choices_whose_target_node_is_gone_before_emission_fold0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 312, "key": "FACT-0431: THE GPU PROTECTION CONTRACT EXISTS AS A FAIL-CLOSED INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN A CHECKLIST: 17 clauses across CODE, DATA, PROCESS and ARTIFACT, with 22 of", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "THE GPU PROTECTION CONTRACT EXISTS AS A FAIL-CLOSED INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN A CHECKLIST: 17 clauses across CODE, DATA, PROCESS and ARTIFACT, with 22 of 22 mutations caught and 21 tests passing, and signing REFUSES outright when the built notebook is absent. Two accept-controls pass, so it is not a reject-everything guard. The contract-2 smoke artifact signs 17 of 17. The clause that would have caught this cycle's own worst near-miss is the capacity guard: a 14-million-node run that the SUPERSEDED 128 bytes-per-node constant WOULD HAVE PASSED is refused, and the test asserts that premise so a regression to the old constant fails loudly rather than silently", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Every clause is proved by a MUTATION that fails without it, not by an assertion that it passes, and two accept-controls establish the instrument is not simply refusing everything - the pairing is what makes either half meaningful. The named limit is recorded in the receipt rather than papered over, which is the distinction FACT-0410 identified as the difference between a skipped check and a satisfied one.", "value": "17 fail_closed_clauses_in_the_pre_launch_gpu_protection_contract"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 313, "key": "FACT-0432: TWO DEFECTS WOULD HAVE MADE A LEVER-0044 GATE B NULL UNINTERPRETABLE, AND BOTH WERE FOUND BY EXERCISING THE CODE RATHER THAN READING IT. (1) THE WIDEN", "observed_at": "2026-08-30", "quote": "TWO DEFECTS WOULD HAVE MADE A LEVER-0044 GATE B NULL UNINTERPRETABLE, AND BOTH WERE FOUND BY EXERCISING THE CODE RATHER THAN READING IT. (1) THE WIDENED-CONTROL GAP IS LIVE: assoc_report.verdict() was called on a report where every channel is favourable and the ONLY defect is the control's identity, and it returned promotable true with blockers empty - build_report validates `control` in no way, and it arrives as an arbitrary spec-supplied path at assoc_train_harness.py:1628. (2) THE COVERAGE HAZARD IS WORSE THAN THE RANGE HAZARD IT WAS MISTAKEN FOR: at notebook line 1652 learned_edge_probs.get((source_id, target_id), 0.0) gives an UNCOVERED pair the WORST score rather than a neutral one, so partial coverage over a widened surface actively penalises every uncovered candidate and an arm fails on COVERAGE while its mechanism is sound. The sigmoid at :1659-1661 that was flagged instead is LATENT, because predict_proba already returns values in range", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Defect 1 was EXERCISED rather than read - a report was constructed whose only flaw was the control's identity and the verdict function passed it - which is the difference between \"no guard is visible in the source\" and \"the guard does not exist\". Defect 2 was read at the named deployed line and its supposed sibling, the range hazard, was checked and found LATENT, so the two are correctly ranked instead of both being reported as live.", "value": "0.0 default_score_given_to_a_pair_the_learned_map_does_not_cover_at_notebook_line_1652"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 314, "key": "FACT-0433: THE WIDENED-CONTROL GAP IS CLOSED, AND THE CLOSURE IS PROVED IN THE EXACT SHAPE THAT DEFEATED THE OLD GUARD. assoc_report.verdict() now fails closed o", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE WIDENED-CONTROL GAP IS CLOSED, AND THE CLOSURE IS PROVED IN THE EXACT SHAPE THAT DEFEATED THE OLD GUARD. assoc_report.verdict() now fails closed on control identity - placed in verdict() and not only in build_report, because FACT-0432 defect 1 was established by calling verdict() DIRECTLY on a hand-built all-favourable report, so a check confined to build_report would have left that path open. Five worlds were CONSTRUCTED rather than asserted, and in all FOUR rejecting worlds every metric channel still reads favourable while promotable is False: the deployed control passes; a byte-identical copy at a different path passes, so the binding is to CONTENT not path; a widened control with favourable metrics FAILS; a tampered control FAILS, including a variant that forges the original sha256; and a missing receipt or any one of the four identity fields FAILS", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Every world is CONSTRUCTED and exercised rather than asserted, and the accept controls (worlds 1 and 2) are what establish this is not a reject-everything guard. The decisive design choice is testable and was tested: the four rejecting worlds each carry FAVOURABLE metrics on every channel, so the only thing producing the refusal is control identity - which is precisely the configuration that returned promotable true before the fix.", "value": "5 constructed_control_binding_worlds_four_of_which_must_reject"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 315, "key": "FACT-0434: THE TWO TRUNK-LEGITIMACY GUARDS NOW AGREE FROM ONE SOURCE, ACROSS A 12-CELL FOLD-BY-PAIR MATRIX WITH EVERY CELL AGREEING. The divergence was repaired ", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE TWO TRUNK-LEGITIMACY GUARDS NOW AGREE FROM ONE SOURCE, ACROSS A 12-CELL FOLD-BY-PAIR MATRIX WITH EVERY CELL AGREEING. The divergence was repaired by RETIRING the old symbols rather than correcting them - PKT0029_REQUIRED_TRUNK_ROLES, INVALID_PAIR and LEGITIMATE_TRUNKS are gone and a test asserts their absence - and replacing them with one shared policy both audit_feature_cache and gpu_protection_contract consume. Both fold-swap directions are rejected by BOTH guards, and in the fold-0 direction the mutation deliberately uses the fold-0 weights glob so the pre-existing glob check CANNOT fire and the policy is the only thing rejecting. A monkeypatch of the policy alone moves both guards, which is what separates one shared source from two coincidentally-equal constants", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The agreement is demonstrated over a complete 12-cell matrix rather than on the one pair that previously diverged, and the single-source claim is proved by INTERVENTION - patching the policy alone moves both guards - which is the only evidence that distinguishes a shared source from two constants that happen to be equal. The fold-0 mutation was deliberately constructed so a pre-existing check could not take the credit.", "value": "12 fold_by_pair_cells_where_both_guards_return_the_same_verdict"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 316, "key": "FACT-0435: FOUR TRUNK CHECKPOINT DIGESTS RE-DERIVED IN FULL FROM THE BYTES, where the registry had held only 16-hex prefixes. oof_split0 is d3e89eb361eeadef06d18", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "FOUR TRUNK CHECKPOINT DIGESTS RE-DERIVED IN FULL FROM THE BYTES, where the registry had held only 16-hex prefixes. oof_split0 is d3e89eb361eeadef06d18159d834594776174a9f8cabd81f65271abbb42a492f at 8,357,783 bytes and is THE SAME BYTES as C:/temp/hoct/trunks/official_f0/edge_predictor_best.pth, independently re-confirming FACT-0418's provenance retraction; oof_split1 is 2e4ebf616b3d4fb53881eadf42c7972e04978c28f74f229c5cb30bee835063de at 8,357,783 bytes; stabledet is 32d8048692aeb95fecd0245758a6b5b68889a84af4c4afc610414ae6fccb6fe4; and pack_split0 is 12f6881ee3620a831697ca098ff8f48e687a24225f4e048b538deec3562fe771 at 8,363,159 bytes - a DIFFERENT byte size, so it is a genuinely different checkpoint rather than a re-hash of the same one", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The first two were hashed from the bytes this cycle and are VERIFIED; the last two are carried from the P37 trunk inventory and are MEASURED, and the distinction is preserved rather than levelled up. The byte-size difference on pack_split0 is what rules out the possibility that it is the OOF checkpoint under another name - a check that matters here precisely because two of the four DID turn out to be the same bytes under different names.", "value": "4 trunk_checkpoints_with_full_sha256_re_derived_from_the_bytes"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 317, "key": "FACT-0436: A COMMITTED TEST IS INVERTED BY THE NEW POLICY AND IT IS RECORDED SO IT IS NEVER READ AS AN UNNOTICED LOOSENING: on fold 0 the trunk pair (pack_split0", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "A COMMITTED TEST IS INVERTED BY THE NEW POLICY AND IT IS RECORDED SO IT IS NEVER READ AS AN UNNOTICED LOOSENING: on fold 0 the trunk pair (pack_split0, official) is now ACCEPTED, where the retired constant refused it. The PKT-0029 mechanism is intact - what FACT-0392's third risk actually requires is TWO DIFFERENT CHECKPOINTS over ONE detector pass in ONE session, so trunk identity can never be confounded with contract error - and what was dropped is only the extra clause demanding the two be named 'official' and 'stabledet' specifically", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The inversion is stated by the packet that caused it rather than discovered later by someone reading a changed test, which is the only reason it is safe: an inverted assertion that nobody announces is indistinguishable from a guard quietly relaxed. Both inverted assertions were re-stated AS inversions in the test file.", "value": "1 committed_tests_whose_verdict_is_inverted_by_the_shared_provenance_policy"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 318, "key": "FACT-0437: GATE A IS NEGATIVE ON THE BOTH-FOLDS REQUIREMENT, AND THE TWO FOLDS DISAGREE MONOTONICALLY IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS. Sweeping MOTION_RELINK_LEARNED_BONU", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "GATE A IS NEGATIVE ON THE BOTH-FOLDS REQUIREMENT, AND THE TWO FOLDS DISAGREE MONOTONICALLY IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS. Sweeping MOTION_RELINK_LEARNED_BONUS over the preregistered grid [0, 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8] with the DEPLOYED edge_prob and DEPLOYED surface unchanged, through the complete deployed chain and the official patched scorer, on ALL 71 fold-0 and ALL 128 fold-1 crops with zero refusals: fold 0 improves MONOTONICALLY with the bonus while fold 1 improves at no value. At bonus 8 fold 0 gains +0.005125 RAW edge Jaccard, +51 net true edges, 64 FEWER false positives and +0.001262 node recall, with a crop-paired interval [+0.00223, +0.00821] excluding zero favourably; fold 1 at the same value loses 0.000743 raw with an interval spanning zero and division TP down 1. NO bonus wins on both folds, so selected_bonus is null. Per the host's amendment recorded before any data, this kills ONLY \"amplify the deployed score\" and says NOTHING about LEVER-0044", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Complete grid, complete both folds, zero refusals, through the OFFICIAL patched scorer at the FULL CHAIN rather than a pre-ILP proxy - so this is the genuine FACT-0376 quantity and not the proxy that every prior association number in this campaign was measured at. The deployed bonus reproduces the control exactly by construction, which is what makes the treated arms interpretable. Raw and adjusted channels move together with a count contribution at most 1.5e-05, so the shape that killed LEVER-0036 and LEVER-0037 is measured absent rather than assumed absent.", "value": "0.005125 fold0_raw_edge_jaccard_delta_at_bonus_8_the_best_single_fold_arm"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 319, "key": "FACT-0438: FOLD 0 CAN RESOLVE AN INTERVENTION AT THE FULL-CHAIN STAGE, SO FACT-0420's POWER COLLAPSE IS A PROPERTY OF THE PRE-ILP CONTESTED-RANKING MEASUREMENT A", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "FOLD 0 CAN RESOLVE AN INTERVENTION AT THE FULL-CHAIN STAGE, SO FACT-0420's POWER COLLAPSE IS A PROPERTY OF THE PRE-ILP CONTESTED-RANKING MEASUREMENT AND NOT OF THE FOLD-0 SURFACE ITSELF. LEVER-0044's restored clause (g) - that the fold-0 arm would reproduce FACT-0414's exact zero at the full chain - DOES NOT FIRE. Only the deployed bonus nets exactly zero, which it must by construction; every treated arm moves fold-0 net true edges away from zero at -36, -10, +31, +42 and +51, and three of the five carry crop-paired intervals excluding zero favourably", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured on the same complete fold-0 surface, all 71 crops, that produced FACT-0420's null - so the difference is the STAGE and not the sample. The clause was restored by an adversarial auditor BEFORE this run and it is answered by it, which is the sequence that makes the answer worth something.", "value": "False whether_the_fold0_full_chain_arm_reproduces_the_exact_zero_of_fact_0414"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 320, "key": "FACT-0439: LEDGER CATEGORY 5 IS NO LONGER PROVISIONAL AND THE BONUS IS THE LEVER ON IT, WHILE CATEGORY 3 IS IMMOVABLE BY THIS MECHANISM. An independent replay re", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "LEDGER CATEGORY 5 IS NO LONGER PROVISIONAL AND THE BONUS IS THE LEVER ON IT, WHILE CATEGORY 3 IS IMMOVABLE BY THIS MECHANISM. An independent replay reproduces FACT-0422's fold-0 partition EXACTLY - 161 / 198 / 1,110 / 240 / 73 / 0 / 18,044 - and under the bonus sweep fold-0 category 5 falls 73 -> 66 -> 60 -> 56 while category 4 falls 240 -> 226 -> 221 -> 216 and CATEGORY 3 DOES NOT MOVE AT ALL. Category 5 IS the motion_relink overwrite, confirming the stage attribution of FACT-0426, and the never-offered population is untouchable by any change to the final consumer", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The control partition was reproduced EXACTLY by an independent replay before any treated arm was read, which is what licenses reading the treated partitions as the same measurement rather than an adjacent one. Category 3 holding fixed across the entire sweep is a strong internal control: a mechanism that changes only the final selector cannot change what was never offered, and if category 3 had moved the ledger would have been wrong.", "value": "0 change_in_ledger_category_3_under_the_entire_bonus_sweep"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 321, "key": "FACT-0440: THE FULL-CHAIN REPLAY IS MEMORY-BOUND, NOT CORE-BOUND, ON THIS MACHINE: the 16 GB box PAGES above THREE concurrent workers, and eight workers cut thro", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE FULL-CHAIN REPLAY IS MEMORY-BOUND, NOT CORE-BOUND, ON THIS MACHINE: the 16 GB box PAGES above THREE concurrent workers, and eight workers cut throughput to ONE FIFTH. Naive core-count parallelism is therefore actively harmful here. A cross-run DeepCenter heatmap cache, validated byte-identical, cuts per-crop replay from 604 s to 175 s - a 3.45x saving that is available without any additional hardware", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured on the real workload on this machine rather than inferred from core count, and the cache saving was validated byte-identical rather than assumed lossless - which matters because a cache that changed the result would have been a silent contamination of every arm downstream of it.", "value": "3 maximum_concurrent_full_chain_replay_workers_before_this_16gb_machine_pages"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 322, "key": "FACT-0441: TWO THIRDS OF LEDGER CATEGORY 3 IS ALREADY IN THE EMITTED GRAPH, SO THE NEVER-OFFERED PRIZE IS FAR SMALLER THAN FACT-0422 IMPLIED. 713 of 1,110 fold-0", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "TWO THIRDS OF LEDGER CATEGORY 3 IS ALREADY IN THE EMITTED GRAPH, SO THE NEVER-OFFERED PRIZE IS FAR SMALLER THAN FACT-0422 IMPLIED. 713 of 1,110 fold-0 (64.2%) and 9,522 of 14,007 fold-1 (68.0%) never-offered GT edges are PRESENT in the deployed emitted graph. The mechanism is verified at deployed source: motion_relink_edges assigns over ALL NODE PAIRS inside a 6.0 um gate rather than over candidate edges, so it routinely emits pairs the candidate rule never proposed. Category 3 therefore describes the CANDIDATE SURFACE, not the emitted graph. Genuinely lost never-offered mass is 397 on fold 0 and 4,485 on fold 1 - so on fold 0 the never-offered prize is 1.65x the wrong-parent prize, NOT 4.6x, and on fold 1 it is 2.58x, not 8.1x", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Established two independent ways that agree. The mechanism was read at named deployed lines rather than inferred from the counts, and the counts were then cross-checked against the OFFICIAL SCORER'S OWN control edge_fn - which reconciles to within 61 and 574 edges once the already-emitted mass is removed, the residual being the two independent matchings. A count-only finding would have been much weaker; a mechanism-only reading would not have given the magnitude.", "value": "397 genuinely_lost_never_offered_gt_edges_fold_0_after_removing_those_already_emitted"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 323, "key": "FACT-0442: LEVER-0045's FALSIFIER 0 FIRES AND THE ROUTE CLOSES BEFORE ANY GPU. A GT-free tracklet-conditioned proposal rule, frozen and hashed BEFORE ground trut", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "LEVER-0045's FALSIFIER 0 FIRES AND THE ROUTE CLOSES BEFORE ANY GPU. A GT-free tracklet-conditioned proposal rule, frozen and hashed BEFORE ground truth was read, reaches 0.4181 of genuinely lost category-3 edges on fold 0 (context 5) and 0.3677 on fold 1 (context 8) at candidate multipliers of 1.28x and 1.38x - but the oracle score contribution under PERFECT selection is only +0.015207 on fold 0 and +0.020375 on fold 1, which is 0.84x and 1.13x the remaining deficit against a preregistered threshold of 2x. ALL SIX CELLS KILL. The best cell reaches 57% of the threshold and the honest promotion fold does not clear even the bare-pass line that was itself preregistered as a kill", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The rule was frozen and HASHED before ground truth was read, with the hash recorded in the packet before the measurement module existed and re-checked on every run - so this is not a rule fitted to the answer. The gate and cap were taken from deployed source and from the setting a killed lever already used, not chosen; the distance code passed the FACT-0040 calibration anchor BEFORE anything derived from it was trusted; and the kill threshold with its 2x margin was preregistered with a stated justification. Complete folds, official scorer.", "value": "0.84 fold0_oracle_contribution_as_a_multiple_of_the_remaining_deficit_against_a_threshold_of_2"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 324, "key": "FACT-0443: DIVISION JACCARD FALLS ON FOLD 1 UNDER PERFECT NEVER-OFFERED SELECTION, so FACT-0371's safety condition fails AT THE ORACLE rather than merely in depl", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "DIVISION JACCARD FALLS ON FOLD 1 UNDER PERFECT NEVER-OFFERED SELECTION, so FACT-0371's safety condition fails AT THE ORACLE rather than merely in deployment: -0.0144, -0.0163 and -0.0160 at contexts 2, 5 and 8. The mechanism is structural - re-parenting a target STRIPS A CHILD EDGE from its previous source, so inserting a correct parent edge can destroy a correct fork", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured through the official scorer's own division term on complete folds, under the same oracle that produced FACT-0442, so the edge gain and the division loss are computed on identical edits rather than on separately-optimised ones. That is what makes them comparable and what makes the safety failure attributable to the insertions themselves.", "value": "-0.0163 fold1_division_jaccard_delta_at_context_5_under_perfect_selection"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 325, "key": "FACT-0444: THE CAMPAIGN'S SUBMISSION-SCORE TRAJECTORY, REGISTERED ONCE SO IT CANNOT BE QUOTED AMBIGUOUSLY AGAIN. Across 18 scored submissions from 2026-07-31 to ", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE CAMPAIGN'S SUBMISSION-SCORE TRAJECTORY, REGISTERED ONCE SO IT CANNOT BE QUOTED AMBIGUOUSLY AGAIN. Across 18 scored submissions from 2026-07-31 to 2026-08-30 the public score moved 0.913 to 0.932: +0.019 over 30 days. The climb is STEP-SHAPED, not linear - 0.915 held flat for roughly 19 days before 0.925 / 0.928 / 0.931 / 0.932 arrived in the final week. THIS SUPERSEDES THE RECENT-WINDOW STATEMENT of \"+0.004 per 26 days\", which was the last THREE submissions presented as the campaign rate and is wrong by about 4.75x", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read directly from the competition's own submissions endpoint, which is the authority for scores, rather than assembled from packet prose. The correction was found by pulling the full list instead of the tail, and it is recorded with BOTH the right number and the wrong one so neither can be cited without the other.", "value": "0.019 public_score_gained_over_the_whole_campaign_2026_07_31_to_2026_08_30"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 326, "key": "FACT-0445: THE OFFICIAL HOCT RELEASE IS NOT ANY CHECKPOINT WE HOLD, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT ARTIFACT CLASS. The royerlab/hoct release `weights-v1` (published 2026-", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE OFFICIAL HOCT RELEASE IS NOT ANY CHECKPOINT WE HOLD, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT ARTIFACT CLASS. The royerlab/hoct release `weights-v1` (published 2026-08-24) ships `general_v1.pt` at 25,496,698 bytes, sha256 5bd836dfcb15ad796ea79a9595841a3e73b650a71c4acba3fc66aac65d745b33, under an MIT licence (Copyright 2026 Jordao Bragantini and the HOCT contributors). It is a TORCHSCRIPT JIT ARCHIVE - a zip of 528 entries including a `code/` tree - whereas every HOCT-family checkpoint on our disk is a plain state-dict of about 8.36 MB. The \"is the public checkpoint identical to one we already have\" question therefore resolves NO", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The file was downloaded read-only and hashed, and its type was determined by inspecting the ZIP directory WITHOUT loading it - so the classification rests on the bytes rather than on the release notes. The negative identity conclusion is arithmetic, not inference: 25,496,698 bytes cannot be the same artifact as an 8.36 MB state dict.", "value": "25496698 bytes_of_the_official_hoct_general_v1_checkpoint"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 327, "key": "FACT-0446: THE FIRST SUBMISSION UNDER THE NEW POLICY IS BOUND AND ITS ARTIFACT IS PROVABLY COMPLETE RATHER THAN ASSUMED COMPLETE. Kaggle reference 55915569, subm", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE FIRST SUBMISSION UNDER THE NEW POLICY IS BOUND AND ITS ARTIFACT IS PROVABLY COMPLETE RATHER THAN ASSUMED COMPLETE. Kaggle reference 55915569, submitted 2026-08-31 12:39:40 from kernel aryaarun07/biohub-p38-relink-bonus-b2 version 1. The in-kernel heartbeat reported rows=237716 bytes=12373010 sha256=786ccf1b72a65bb0ec7a1ce21390a5fe30edd952d9bae701d9b48d23964cf12a and the fetched file's byte count and sha256 MATCH IT EXACTLY, so the atomic-write instrumentation the auditor required demonstrably worked. The treatment is confirmed LIVE in the immutable log at motion_relink_learned_bonus 2.0, not the base 1.0. Structural audit PASS 10 of 10", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Every element is bound to bytes rather than asserted: the artifact's sha256 is reported by the kernel itself and independently recomputed on the fetched file and they agree; the treatment is read from the immutable log rather than from the spec that requested it; and the preregistration was committed to git BEFORE the artifact existed, so the band cannot have been fitted to a result that did not yet exist. The SCORE is deliberately PENDING - this entry records the submission, not its outcome.", "value": "55915569 kaggle_submission_reference_of_the_first_submission_under_the_q2_policy"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 328, "key": "FACT-0447: THE REVERSED CEILING LADDER: NODE CORRECTION AT TODAY'S ASSOCIATION IS WORTH EXACTLY ZERO FULL-CHAIN SCORE ON BOTH FOLDS. Inserting every annotated GT", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE REVERSED CEILING LADDER: NODE CORRECTION AT TODAY'S ASSOCIATION IS WORTH EXACTLY ZERO FULL-CHAIN SCORE ON BOTH FOLDS. Inserting every annotated GT cell the deployed pipeline misses - 223 on fold 0 and 14,970 on fold 1 - takes node recall from 0.98679 to 1.00000 and from 0.86357 to 1.00000 while changing edge TP, FP and FN by EXACTLY ZERO on both folds; count-fair delta score is +0.000000 on both. Under a frozen consumer a newly detected cell arrives as an ORPHAN, so detection recall converts to score at a rate of ZERO. Perfect LOCALISATION of already-matched nodes under frozen topology is slightly NEGATIVE: -0.000364 count-fair score on fold 0 and -0.000043 on fold 1, moving 3 and 2 true edges into errors", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Three calibration gates passed BEFORE any arm was read, and the coordinate gate was built to DISCRIMINATE rather than merely to pass - the isotropic convention that has twice been used by mistake in this project fails it at 5.13870 um against the FACT-0040 anchor. The instrument's own perfect-nodes-plus-perfect-edges arm returns exactly 1.000000 on both folds, matching FACT-0368's harness, and the control reproduces the FACT-0368 / FACT-0371 anchors to 1e-9 on floats and exactly on counts, with three further registry cross-checks landing unprompted.", "value": "0.0 count_fair_score_delta_from_perfect_node_membership_at_frozen_association_both_folds"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 329, "key": "FACT-0448: NEARLY EVERY FALSE-POSITIVE EDGE THIS PIPELINE EMITS POINTS AT AN UNANNOTATED NODE. Of 1,369 fold-0 false-positive edges only SIXTEEN are wrong links ", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "NEARLY EVERY FALSE-POSITIVE EDGE THIS PIPELINE EMITS POINTS AT AN UNANNOTATED NODE. Of 1,369 fold-0 false-positive edges only SIXTEEN are wrong links between two ANNOTATED cells; the other 1,353 - 98.8% - run from an annotated cell into an unannotated one. On fold 1 it is 86 of 13,946, or 0.6%, with 13,860 running into unannotated nodes", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Falls directly out of the perfect-membership arm, which by construction retains every edge whose endpoints both match an annotated cell - so the residual is exactly the between-annotated population and is counted rather than estimated. Measured on complete folds through the official one-to-one 7 um matcher.", "value": "16 fold0_false_positive_edges_between_two_annotated_cells"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 330, "key": "FACT-0449: THE DEPLOYED CHAIN UNDER-PRODUCES NODES AT THE EMITTED GRAPH, NOT ONLY AT THE DETECTION SURFACE: N_pred/N_est is 0.7275 on fold 0 and 0.9171 on fold 1", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE DEPLOYED CHAIN UNDER-PRODUCES NODES AT THE EMITTED GRAPH, NOT ONLY AT THE DETECTION SURFACE: N_pred/N_est is 0.7275 on fold 0 and 0.9171 on fold 1, measured on the FINAL EMITTED GRAPH over complete folds - 1,905,264 of 2,618,970 and 1,931,622 of 2,106,147", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Measured on the emitted graph over complete folds with N_est taken from the scorer's own quantity rather than reconstructed, so it is the ratio the metric actually applies.", "value": "0.7275 n_pred_over_n_est_on_the_emitted_graph_fold_0"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 331, "key": "FACT-0450: THE REVERSED-LADDER HARNESS IS CHEAP AND FACT-0440's THREE-WORKER CEILING IS NOT A BLANKET MACHINE LIMIT: 199 crop-arms across both complete folds in ", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE REVERSED-LADDER HARNESS IS CHEAP AND FACT-0440's THREE-WORKER CEILING IS NOT A BLANKET MACHINE LIMIT: 199 crop-arms across both complete folds in about 8 minutes of wall clock at three workers - roughly 1,235 crops/hour on fold 0 and 1,726 on fold 1 - with free RAM never below 4.5 GB and zero refusals. A fourth worker, tested as a controlled A/B on one fixed 48-crop set, bought only about 9% (93 s against 101 s) without paging, and was NOT adopted", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The fourth-worker question was settled by a CONTROLLED A/B on one fixed crop set rather than by comparing two different workloads, and determinism was confirmed by regenerating a subset under a different worker count and getting an identical panel. The concurrent second agent is named as a confound rather than ignored.", "value": "3 workers_used_for_the_delivered_reversed_ladder_result"}
{"claim_type": "claim", "confidence": "low", "id": 332, "key": "FACT-0451: THE TRAINING DATA OF HOCT's general_v1.pt CANNOT BE ESTABLISHED, AND OVERLAP WITH THE COMPETITION MOVIES OR THEIR SOURCES CANNOT BE EXCLUDED. The pape", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE TRAINING DATA OF HOCT's general_v1.pt CANNOT BE ESTABLISHED, AND OVERLAP WITH THE COMPETITION MOVIES OR THEIR SOURCES CANNOT BE EXCLUDED. The paper documents 16 named Cell Tracking Challenge datasets, none zebrafish - but for THE PAPER's models; general_v1 is not one of them, the paper predates it by six weeks and names no \"general\" model, and it is described only as \"for general datasets\". No manifest, model card, release note, pull request, commit message, repo tree entry or issue names its data, and its producing package `slot_cell_tracking` is unpublished. The prior is ADVERSE: the publisher is the ORGANIZER LAB and the asset was released eight weeks into the competition. CONSEQUENCE, recorded before any number exists: general_v1 is RESTRICTED TO SUBMISSION-ONLY JUDGEMENT", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "THIS IS THE ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE AND IT IS LABELLED AS SUCH. The search was finished rather than abandoned - manifest, card, release body, PRs, commits, tree and issues were all checked and all are silent - but a completed search of public surfaces cannot establish what a model was trained on. It is WEAKER evidence than FACT-0424's, not stronger: there a curated inventory existed to check against, here there is none. STRENGTHENED 2026-08-31 BY OUR OWN DATED EVIDENCE, which converts the residual from unexamined to CHECKED. This project snapshotted HOCT's README on 2026-08-07 - seventeen days BEFORE general_v1 shipped and before this lane existed - at _evidence/agent_runs/v7_diagnostic_20260807/researchR3/sources/hoct_README.md, digest 7def7cc1, reproducing exactly from the bytes. In it general_v1 has ZERO mentions, ctc_v0 ZERO, general_v0 two. Decisively, its Pre-trained models section names NO MODELS AT ALL - only the download-and-verify mechanism - and every per-model description, including \"the default model for general datasets\", was ADDED BY PR 4 on 2026-08-24, the same commit that registered general_v1. So NOTHING WAS EVER DELETED: the publisher has never, at any point in the repository's history, described the training data of any general checkpoint. The \"perhaps an earlier README said more\" residual is now a checked negative, and the release timing no longer rests on GitHub's own timestamps alone.", "value": "False whether_overlap_with_competition_data_can_be_excluded_for_hoct_general_v1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 333, "key": "FACT-0452: HOCT's general_v1.pt IS ADMISSIBLE UNDER THIS COMPETITION'S OWN RULE TEXT, AND NO DOCUMENT ANYWHERE ASSERTS A LICENCE OVER THE WEIGHTS. The rules were", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "HOCT's general_v1.pt IS ADMISSIBLE UNDER THIS COMPETITION'S OWN RULE TEXT, AND NO DOCUMENT ANYWHERE ASSERTS A LICENCE OVER THE WEIGHTS. The rules were re-obtained and re-authenticated this cycle - 36,552 bytes, sha256 6d025a6e, matched field by field against a freshly fetched GetCompetition RPC - and the deciding clauses are 2.6.a, 2.6.b and 2.5.a.3 as for FOCUS-3D, plus 3.6.c which FOCUS-3D did not need: an OSI-approved licence that does not limit commercial use, which MIT satisfies and the fork bundle's CC BY 4.0 weights do not. The repository has exactly ONE licence artifact, but the CHECKPOINT embeds TorchScript-compiled timm under Apache-2.0, surfaced nowhere by the publisher", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The rules were re-authenticated against an independent RPC payload BEFORE being quoted, rather than trusted from a page fetch, and the licence position was read from the repository's single LICENSE commit and from the artifact's own embedded package rather than from a badge. The negative - that no document asserts a licence over the weights - is the result of a finished search, and it is recorded as a gap rather than resolved by assumption.", "value": "3 licence_obligations_binding_a_hoct_general_v1_integration"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 334, "key": "FACT-0453: HOCT's general_v1.pt IS A SELF-CONTAINED EDGE MODEL THAT NEEDS NO TRUNK, AND ITS PARAMETER COUNT WAS TAKEN WITHOUT EVER EXECUTING IT. By pickle-opcode", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "HOCT's general_v1.pt IS A SELF-CONTAINED EDGE MODEL THAT NEEDS NO TRUNK, AND ITS PARAMETER COUNT WAS TAKEN WITHOUT EVER EXECUTING IT. By pickle-opcode disassembly and an inert-stub unpickler it is slot_cell_tracking.modules.edge_model.EdgeModel with 132 tensors and 6,294,081 elements - calibrated independently, since its 25,176,324 raw storage bytes are exactly four times that count. C=288, four heads, four node and four edge blocks, two Linear(19->288) inputs, timm RmsNorm, RoPE at edge midpoints, a LEARNED SOFTPLUS DISTANCE PRIOR added to the attention mask, head Linear(288->1). It is a DIFFERENT MODEL from FACT-0390's 447,376-parameter fork head, and because it needs no trunk, FACT-0392's GPU-bound trunk-feature blocker and its trunk-identity confound DO NOT APPLY", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read by pickle-opcode disassembly and an inert-stub unpickler, so the archived TorchScript graph was never EXECUTED - which was the binding constraint while training provenance and eligibility were unsettled. The count is not a single reading: it is calibrated against the raw storage size, which is exactly four bytes per element, so a mis-parse would not have produced an exact ratio.", "value": "6294081 parameter_elements_in_hoct_general_v1"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 335, "key": "FACT-0454: TWO ADAPTER BLOCKERS FOR HOCT v0.2.0, BOTH VERIFIED AT file:line AND BOTH SILENT. FIRST, THE `scale` ARGUMENT NEVER REACHES THE MODEL: `scaled_` occur", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "TWO ADAPTER BLOCKERS FOR HOCT v0.2.0, BOTH VERIFIED AT file:line AND BOTH SILENT. FIRST, THE `scale` ARGUMENT NEVER REACHES THE MODEL: `scaled_` occurs exactly once in the whole package, at graph.py:182, into a local frame that is discarded; graph.py:143 defaults it to 1.0; graph.py:212 records it in metadata only AFTER DistanceEdges has already run at graph.py:191; and _frame_dataset.py:54 feeds the raw z,y,x columns. The paper corroborates with \"tau = 300 PIXELS\". HOCT IS VOXEL-NATIVE, so on our 4:1:1 anisotropic data neither microns nor raw voxels is safe by default. SECOND, 15 OF THE 19 INPUT FEATURES REQUIRE INSTANCE MASKS the deployed notebook does not produce, and the one published points-only entry point is an unimplemented stub that is nonetheless exported", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Both were read at named lines in the published package at a pinned commit, and each was established by a finished search rather than a single grep - the scale finding rests on the SOLE occurrence of the symbol in the entire package plus the ordering of three call sites, and the mask finding on the absence of every segmentation idiom in the deployed notebook together with the stub's own body.", "value": "15 of_19_hoct_input_features_requiring_instance_masks_we_do_not_have"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 336, "key": "FACT-0455: TAU = 300 IS COMPILED INTO general_v1 TWICE AND IS THE MODEL'S COORDINATE UNIT, NOT A TUNABLE THRESHOLD. It appears as the squared attention cutoff `l", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "TAU = 300 IS COMPILED INTO general_v1 TWICE AND IS THE MODEL'S COORDINATE UNIT, NOT A TUNABLE THRESHOLD. It appears as the squared attention cutoff `lt(elem_pdist, 90000.)` over BOTH node_pos and edge_pos, and as the RoPE positional normaliser CONSTANTS.c0 = 300.0 with c2 = sqrt(3), where the compiled RoPE computes node_pos / c0. Read from the TorchScript archive as text and as raw bytes; torch.jit.load and pickle.load were NEVER called. Consequently the 19-slot input order is also fixed and independently cross-checked: t, z, y, x, equivalent_diameter_area, intensity_{min,max,mean,std}, inertia_tensor[0..8] row-major, border_dist", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read from the artifact itself rather than from the paper, and without executing it - the constraint that bound the whole packet. The slot order is not asserted from source reading alone: it is proved four independent ways against the publisher's own shipped _MEAN/_STD, including exact 3x3 symmetry in BOTH statistics and the perpendicular-axis theorem holding to 1.7%, so a mis-ordered map would break at least one of them.", "value": "300.0 hoct_general_v1_compiled_coordinate_unit_tau"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 337, "key": "FACT-0456: NO UNIT CONVENTION FOR OUR 4:1:1 DATA SATISFIES ALL THREE PARTS OF THE HOCT SCALE GATE, AND THAT - NOT THE MISSING MASK FEATURES - IS WHAT BLOCKS THE ", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "NO UNIT CONVENTION FOR OUR 4:1:1 DATA SATISFIES ALL THREE PARTS OF THE HOCT SCALE GATE, AND THAT - NOT THE MISSING MASK FEATURES - IS WHAT BLOCKS THE MASKS-INTO-OFFICIAL-HOCT ROUTE. Microns DISABLE the compiled cutoff entirely (the crop diagonal is 0.60 tau, so it never fires); raw voxels and isotropic-1.625 distort the 300-ball by 4.0x in z; and the only geometrically admissible convention, xy-voxel isotropic, places our z at 32.77 SIGMA of the shipped standardisation. The best available compromise is raw voxels with z RECENTRED, which moves 7.90 sigma to 4.24 at ZERO geometric cost because RoPE plus a Householder reflection make the attention logits translation-invariant", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Part A reproduces the FACT-0040 anchor AND the FACT-0447 isotropic discriminator before any new quantity is read, so the gate is shown to reject before it is used to reject - it turns down 3 of 5 conventions. The parts are independent: geometry (does the compiled cutoff behave) and distribution (is our data inside the shipped standardisation) are different failures, and the finding is that they are ANTI-CORRELATED here rather than that one bar was missed.", "value": "32.77 z_sigma_of_the_shipped_standardisation_under_the_only_geometrically_admissible_convention"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 338, "key": "FACT-0457: general_v1 HAS NO LEARNED ABSTENTION. Output 3 is torch.new_zeros; _predict.py:359 exponentiates it to a constant 1.0 per node; so the abstain mass at", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "general_v1 HAS NO LEARNED ABSTENTION. Output 3 is torch.new_zeros; _predict.py:359 exponentiates it to a constant 1.0 per node; so the abstain mass at _predict.py:426-428 is orphan_prob = 1 / (sum of edge sim_exp + 1) - a DETERMINISTIC FUNCTION OF THE EDGE LOGITS against a hard-coded logit-zero reference, not a separately learned quantity", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Read from the archived source at named lines without executing the model, and consistent with FACT-0453's independent finding that output 3 is a constant zero which the publisher's own code calls \"orphan logits\".", "value": "0.0 learned_parameters_behind_hoct_general_v1_abstention"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 339, "key": "FACT-0458: THE DEPLOYED EMITTED GRAPH LOCALLY OVER-COVERS WHILE GLOBALLY UNDER-PRODUCING. On complete folds, 5,674 of 20,197 annotated cells on fold 0 (28.1%) an", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "THE DEPLOYED EMITTED GRAPH LOCALLY OVER-COVERS WHILE GLOBALLY UNDER-PRODUCING. On complete folds, 5,674 of 20,197 annotated cells on fold 0 (28.1%) and 21,147 of 113,121 on fold 1 (18.7%) carry MORE THAN ONE predicted node within the official 7 um; 200,736 (fold 0) and 195,866 (fold 1) predicted pairs sit within 7 um of each other; while only 450 and 253 predicted nodes carry more than one annotated cell. Read beside FACT-0449's N_pred/N_est of 0.7275 and 0.9171 these do not conflict, and neither may be substituted for the other", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The instrument reproduced four independent registry quantities EXACTLY before any new number was read - FACT-0447's unmatched-GT counts 223 and 14,970, FACT-0449's emitted node counts 1,905,264 and 1,931,622, FACT-0380's division shares, and FACT-0080's 125 fold-1 GT divisions - with a GT-identity self-check returning recall 1.000000 and residual 0.0 on both folds.", "value": "0.281 share_of_fold0_annotated_cells_with_more_than_one_predicted_node_within_7um"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 340, "key": "FACT-0459: A ZERO-FILLED FEATURE SURVIVES EVERY NAIVE GUARD ONCE IT PASSES THROUGH STANDARDISATION, AND THE REFUSAL MUST READ THE ARRAY RATHER THAN THE BOOKKEEPI", "observed_at": "2026-08-31", "quote": "A ZERO-FILLED FEATURE SURVIVES EVERY NAIVE GUARD ONCE IT PASSES THROUGH STANDARDISATION, AND THE REFUSAL MUST READ THE ARRAY RATHER THAN THE BOOKKEEPING. In the HOCT feature contract's mutation suite, a post-Standardize zero fill arrives as the CONSTANT -mean/std - measured at -1.4052 and -0.2473 - on which shape checks, NaN checks and \"no zeros present\" checks ALL PASS. The audit refuses it because it inspects only the array; correct bookkeeping over wrong data cannot fool it, which was demonstrated when it caught THREE defects in its own fixture that were invisible to inspection", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Each arm is a constructed mutation with its own expected verdict, and the decisive arm was built specifically to defeat the obvious guards rather than to pass. The instrument's credibility rests on it having caught three real defects in the fixture it was given, none of which were visible by reading the fixture.", "value": "-1.4052 value_a_post_standardisation_zero_fill_takes_and_which_no_naive_guard_rejects"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 341, "key": "FACT-0460: THE RELEASED FOCUS-3D NUCLEI CHECKPOINT MATCHES EVERY INFERENCE-RUNTIME STATE KEY, SHAPE AND DTYPE. The raw strict comparison has exactly one checkpoi", "observed_at": "2026-09-01", "quote": "THE RELEASED FOCUS-3D NUCLEI CHECKPOINT MATCHES EVERY INFERENCE-RUNTIME STATE KEY, SHAPE AND DTYPE. The raw strict comparison has exactly one checkpoint-only tensor, `criterion.empty_weight`; the publisher source registers that exact training-only buffer, the inference builder explicitly omits the criterion, and the tensor values exactly match `NUM_CLASSES` and `NO_OBJECT_WEIGHT` from the pinned config. The checkpoint/runtime contract therefore passes without accepting a wildcard or hiding a missing inference parameter.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Re-derived after commit 6d7ae4d from the released tensor file and the pinned publisher runtime. The instrument separately checks key presence, tensor shapes and dtypes, then binds the sole allowlisted extra to source bytes and config-derived values. Mutation tests reject missing, arbitrary-extra, shape, dtype, source and value drift independently.", "value": "True checkpoint_runtime_contract_clean"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 342, "key": "FACT-0461: ON THE PINNED XET-BACKED FOCUS-3D RELEASE, `x-linked-etag` IS NOT THE SHA-256 OF THE DOWNLOADED BYTES. The pinned Hugging Face API tree's `lfs.oid` ma", "observed_at": "2026-09-01", "quote": "ON THE PINNED XET-BACKED FOCUS-3D RELEASE, `x-linked-etag` IS NOT THE SHA-256 OF THE DOWNLOADED BYTES. The pinned Hugging Face API tree's `lfs.oid` matches the measured file digest and is the authoritative identity. Comparing downloaded bytes to the Xet header falsely refuses a correct complete artifact; loosening digest verification to make that refusal disappear would remove the real guard.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "Re-derived from the pinned release receipt and made mechanical at commit b3dfcdf. Mutation tests accept a valid file when the Xet header differs, refuse a missing or malformed lfs.oid even when the header looks like a SHA-256, refuse wrong bytes, and refuse an ambiguous API tree match.", "value": "False x_linked_etag_equals_downloaded_file_sha256"}
{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 343, "key": "FACT-0462: THE CURRENT FULL-SUITE FAILURES ARE OUTSIDE THE BIOHUB-X RUNTIME IMPORT BOUNDARY, BUT THEY STILL BLOCK A GPU SMOKE. Two failures are stale association", "observed_at": "2026-09-01", "quote": "THE CURRENT FULL-SUITE FAILURES ARE OUTSIDE THE BIOHUB-X RUNTIME IMPORT BOUNDARY, BUT THEY STILL BLOCK A GPU SMOKE. Two failures are stale association-harness fixtures missing the new mandatory restriction field; the remainder exercise the separate provenance-policy guard. A committed AST instrument proves that no Biohub-X module imports either live Gate B surface or the failing provenance/restriction modules. This is an explicit temporary isolation record, not a claim that a red full suite is acceptable.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 54, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "prior-campaign", "validity": "VALID", "validity_reason": "The full suite identified exactly these two test modules; the focused Biohub-X/FOCUS/Xet suite passes, and the committed AST test parses every Biohub-X module without importing it and refuses any dependency on the named association, Gate B, restriction, or protection surfaces. The suite remains a launch gate: phase 3 cannot consume GPU until it is green.", "value": "16 full_suite_failures_at_biohubx_phase_2_boundary"}
