{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "id": 385, "key": "colab_budget", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "T4: approximately 1.76 compute units per hour; A100: approximately 15 compute units per hour", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": null, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "hardware", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "Legacy fact has no source or quote; recover the original evidence before relying on it", "value": "~1000 Colab compute units. Burn rates approx: A100 ~12-15 units/hr, L4 ~4.8/hr, T4 ~1.76/hr. So the budget is roughly 65-85 h of A100, ~200 h of L4, or ~500 h of T4. A100 is ~10x the M5 Pro's estimated FP16 and ~5x its memory bandwidth (1555 vs 307 GB/s)."}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "id": 386, "key": "compute_ranking", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "A100 BFLOAT16 Tensor Core 312 TFLOPS; T4 Mixed-Precision 65 TFLOPS", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": null, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "hardware", "validity": "SUSPECT", "validity_reason": "Legacy fact has no source or quote; recover the original evidence before relying on it", "value": "Raw training throughput, best first: Colab A100 (312 TFLOPS bf16, 40GB, 1555GB/s) >> Kaggle T4 x2 (2x65 TFLOPS mixed, 16GB, 300GB/s) > M5 Pro (est. 33-35 TFLOPS FP16, ~36GB usable, 307GB/s). The Mac is the SLOWEST of the three for training and the only one with no queue and no runtime wall."}
