{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "medium", "id": 496, "key": "gpu_value_ranking", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "The T4 GPU burns through 1.96 units per hour, the V100 uses 5 units per hour, and the A100 demolishes 15 units per hour", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": 67, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "hardware", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "TFLOPS per compute-unit-hour: T4 33.2 (65 TF @1.96 u/h), L4 25.2 (121 TF @4.8), A100 20.8 (312 TF @15). T4 is nominally the best value per unit - BUT Kaggle supplies T4 x2 free for 2x12h/day, so spending Colab units on T4-class compute buys what you already have. L4 is the worst option here: 2.4x the burn of a T4 for the SAME 300 GB/s bandwidth. Colab units should buy only what Kaggle cannot: A100's 40GB and 1555 GB/s (5x the bandwidth), which is what 3D conv training is actually bound by."}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "high", "id": 497, "key": "north_star_0980", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "84 of 151 divisions (55.6%) are recoverable by post-processing alone ... ceiling is 89/151 = 0.589 divJ", "review_after": "2026-12-11", "source_id": 67, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "strategy", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "NORTH STAR 0.980. score = 0.9465 (public edge plateau) + 0.1*divJ. Today rank1=0.970 implies divJ~0.235. 0.980 needs divJ=0.335 - only 57% of the MEASURED post-processing ceiling of 0.589, which needs no new detections at all. divJ 0.40 gives 0.9865; the ceiling gives 1.0054 (scores can exceed 1.0)."}
