{"claim_type": "observation", "confidence": "high", "id": 577, "key": "public_caps_are_the_real_limit", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Division geometry gate: parent-child distance at most 9.0 um (sister max is 14.0 um and existing-child max 10.0 um)", "review_after": null, "source_id": 68, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "CORRECTION to the earlier claim. The CURRENT public 0.947 stack has ALREADY widened the division gates - parent <=9.0um, sister <=14.0um, existing-child <=10.0um - close to the (10,15) the monolith's division_lane report recommended. The 4.7/7.2 constants describe the OLDER 0.918 stack. The binding constraint has moved: forks are throttled to 0.375% of all edges globally and 0.76% of sources per frame, plus a divergence requirement (grandchildren must separate by >=2.25um more than the sisters two frames later) and a DeepCenter heatmap veto at 0.25. So the public divJ is small but NON-zero, not zero. The lever is the FREQUENCY CAP, not the geometry."}
{"claim_type": "inference", "confidence": "high", "id": 578, "key": "ranking_not_cap_is_binding", "observed_at": "2026-09-11", "quote": "Division proposals are ranked by parent distance plus 0.15 times sister distance, cheapest first.", "review_after": null, "source_id": 68, "status": "active", "superseded_by": null, "tbl": "fact", "topic": "division", "validity": "UNKNOWN", "validity_reason": null, "value": "THE LIVE LEVER, refined. The public 0.947 stack caps forks at 0.375% of edges while the true division rate is 1 in 853 = 0.117% - so the cap has 3.2x headroom and is NOT binding. What is binding is the RANKING: it orders candidates by parent_dist + 0.15*sister_dist, cheapest-first, which is exactly inverted against measured GT geometry (true divisions are the wide, angularly-opposed, persistently-diverging pairs at 8.98/11.47um and cos -0.71..-0.76; false forks sit at 3.72um and cos -0.33). They spend a 3x budget entirely on the tightest candidates, which are adjacent unrelated tracks. Fix the ORDER, not the budget or the gates."}
